hadiths[819]{hadithnumber,text}:
"562","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah from Zayd ibn Ali from his father from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah and said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. He departed when the sun set, then took Usamah riding behind him and made gentle pace upon his camel, and the people striking right and left, turning to them and saying: Calmness, O people. Then he came to Jam and prayed with them the two prayers, Maghrib and Isha. Then he spent the night until morning, then came to Quzah and stood upon Quzah and said: This is the standing place, and all of Jam is a standing place. Then he went until he came to Muhassir and stood upon it and struck his she-camel, so it trotted until it crossed the valley, then he restrained it, then took al-Fadl riding behind him and went until he came to the Jamarah and stoned it. Then he came to the slaughter place and said: This is the slaughter place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place. He said: And a young girl of Khatham asked him and said: My father is an old man, advanced in age, and the obligation of Allah in Hajj has reached him, so does it suffice from him that I perform it from him? He said: Yes, perform from your father. He said: And he had twisted the neck of al-Fadl, so al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you twist the neck of your cousin? He said: I saw a young man and a young woman, so I did not feel safe from Satan for them. He said: Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I sacrificed. He said: Sacrifice, no harm. Then another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I performed ifadah before I shaved. He said: Shave or shorten, no harm. Then he came to the House and performed tawaf of it, then came to Zamzam and said: O sons of Abdulmuttalib, your watering, and were it not that the people would overcome you upon it, I would have drawn with it."
"563","Abdussamad ibn Abdulwarith narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The urine of a boy is sprinkled upon, and the urine of a girl is washed. Qatadah said: This is while they have not eaten; if they have eaten, the urine of both is washed."
"564","Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us who said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Basri narrated to me: Al-Mughirah ibn Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us: My father Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Zayd ibn Ali ibn Husayn ibn Ali from his father Ali ibn Husayn from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah while having Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, and said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. Then he moved on traveling at gentle pace, and the people striking right and left, while he turned and said: Calmness, O people. Calmness, O people. Until he came to Muzdalifah and combined the two prayers. Then he stood at Muzdalifah and stood upon Quzah and took al-Fadl ibn Abbas riding behind him, and said: This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place. Then he moved on traveling at gentle pace, and the people striking right and left, while he turned and said: Calmness. Calmness, O people. Until he came to Muhassir, then he struck his mount, so it trotted until it left, then returned to his first pace until he stoned the Jamarah. Then he came to the slaughter place and said: This is the slaughter place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place. Then a young woman of Khatham came to him and said: My father is an old man and has become senile, and the obligation of Allah in Hajj has reached him, yet he cannot perform it, so does it suffice from him that I perform it from him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. And he kept turning the face of al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas from her. Then a man came to him and said: I stoned the Jamarah and performed ifadah and wore clothes and did not shave. He said: No harm, so shave. Then another man came to him and said: I stoned and shaved and wore clothes and did not sacrifice. He said: No harm, so sacrifice. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ifadah, then called for a bucket of Zamzam water, drank from it and performed ablution, then said: Draw, O sons of Abdulmuttalib, for were it not that you would be overcome upon it, I would have drawn. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you turning the face of your nephew. He said: I saw a young boy and a young girl, so I feared Satan for them."
"565","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Harith from Ali who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge for a sick person, he said: Remove the harm, Lord of people. Heal, You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness."
"566","Abu Said narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Harith from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were appointing one without consultation of the believers, I would appoint Ibn Umm Abd."
"567","Abu Said narrated to us: Said ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam, Madinan, freedman of the family of Umar, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah from Amr ibn Sulaym from his mother who said: While we were at Mina, Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, was saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are days of eating and drinking, so no one should fast them. And he followed the people upon his camel shouting with that."
"568","Abu Said narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abdulala narrated to us from Abu Abdurrahman from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he raised it, who said: Whoever lies about his dream will be burdened with tying a barley grain on the Day of Resurrection."
"569","Abu Said and Husayn ibn Muhammad said: Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs of dawn at the iqamah."
"570","Abu Said narrated to us: Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Umarah ibn al-Qaqa narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Ukli from Abu Zurah from Abdullah ibn Nujayy who said: Ali said: I had an hour before dawn in which I would enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If he was standing praying, he would glorify by me, and that was his permission for me, and if he was not praying, he would permit me."
"571","Abdullah narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Abdurrahim from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from al-Zuhri from Ali ibn Husayn from his father who said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was sleeping, I and Fatimah, and that was before dawn, until he stood at the door and said: Will you not pray? So I answered him: O Messenger of Allah, our souls are in the hand of Allah; when He wills to arouse us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and did not return to speech, then I heard him when he turned away saying, striking his thigh with his hand: And man is most argumentative of things."
"572","Abu Said narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family used to bathe from one vessel."
"573","Abu Said narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Simak narrated to us from Hanash from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, so we came to a people who had built a pit for a lion. While they were pushing one another, a man fell and clung to another, then a man clung to another, until they became four in it. The lion wounded them, then a man volunteered for it with a spear and killed it, and they all died of their wounds. So the kin of the first stood against the kin of the last and brought out weapons to fight. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came to them at the subsiding of that and said: Do you want to fight while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is alive? I will judge between you a judgement; if you accept it, it is the judgement, otherwise some of you restrain from others until you come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he is the one who judges between you. Whoever transgresses after that has no right. Gather from the tribes of those who dug the well a quarter of blood money and a third of blood money and half of blood money and complete blood money: For the first a quarter, because those above him perished, and for the second a third of blood money, and for the third half of blood money. But they refused to accept. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the Station of Ibrahim, and told him the story. He said: I will judge between you. And he sat with knees drawn up. A man of the people said: Ali judged among us. So they told him the story, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approved it."
"574","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Simak informed us from Hanash that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: And for the fourth complete blood money."
"575","Abdullah said: Qutaybah ibn Said wrote to me: I wrote to you in my hand and sealed the book with my seal, mentioning that al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to them from Uqayl from al-Zuhri from Ali ibn al-Husayn that al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to him from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knocked upon him and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, and said: Will you not pray? I said: O Messenger of Allah, our souls are in the hand of Allah; when He wills to arouse us He arouses us. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left when I said that to him, then I heard him while turning away striking his thigh and saying: And man is most argumentative of things."
"576","Abdullah narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ali al-Azdi narrated to me: Ali ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali informed me: My brother Musa ibn Jafar narrated to me from his father Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father from Ali ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Hasan and Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: Whoever loves me and loves these two and their father and their mother will be with me in my rank on the Day of Resurrection."
"577","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Hubayrah al-Sabai narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt."
"578","Hasan and Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Zurayr that he said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him - Hasan said: on the day of Adha - so he brought near to us khazirah, so I said: May Allah keep you right, if you brought near to us of this duck, meaning geese, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has multiplied good. He said: O Ibn Zurayr, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for the caliph from the wealth of Allah except two bowls: a bowl he eats, he and his family, and a bowl he puts before the people."
"579","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father from al-Mughirah from Umm Musa from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I have not had eye inflammation since the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in my eye."
"580","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Mutarrif narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Asim from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr in the first of the night and in its middle and in its last, then witr became fixed for him in its last."
"581","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to me: Al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from his mother Fatimah daughter of Husayn from Husayn from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not gaze continuously at lepers, and when you speak to them, let there be between you and them a spear's length."
"582","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us: Al-Qasim ibn Abdurrahman narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ali from his father from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, perfect ablution though it be hard upon you, and do not eat charity, and do not breed donkeys upon horses, and do not sit with astrologers."
"583","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from al-Amash from Abdulmalik ibn Maysarah from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought a jug of water while he was in al-Rahbah, so he took a handful of water and rinsed and sniffed and wiped his face and his forearms and his head, then drank while standing, then said: This is the ablution of one who has not broken purity. Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"584","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from al-Amash from Habib from Thalabah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"585","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Al-Mughirah narrated to us from Umm Musa from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The last speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Prayer. Prayer. Fear Allah regarding what your right hands possess."
"586","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Asim ibn Kulayb from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from Abu Musa from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to put my ring in this forefinger or the one next to it."
"587","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us: Al-Zuhri informed us from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abdurrahman ibn Awf, who said: Then I witnessed Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, after that on a day of Eid beginning with prayer before the sermon, and praying without adhan nor iqamah, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that anyone keep anything of his sacrifice beyond three days."
"588","Abdullah narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me: Ali ibn Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Barid, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Umar ibn Ali ibn Husayn from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his wives choice of this world and the Hereafter, and did not give them choice of divorce."
"589","Abdullah narrated to us who said: And Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated it to us: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, then he mentioned likewise, and said: He gave his wives choice between this world and the Hereafter, and did not give them choice of divorce."
"590","Abu Yusuf the teacher Yaqub our neighbor narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us from Abdulaziz ibn al-Muttalib from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith from Zayd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"591","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Said from Qatadah from Abu Hassan from Abidah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Confederates: May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire as they distracted us from prayer until the sun set."
"592","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from al-Hasan and Abdullah, sons of Muhammad ibn Ali, from their father - and Hasan was the more pleasing of them in our view - that Ali said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys at the time of Khaybar."
"593","Sufyan narrated to us from Abdulkarim from Mujahid from Ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to distribute his sacrificial camels, standing over them, and to distribute their skins and their coverings, and commanded me not to give the butcher anything from them, and said: We give him from ourselves."
"594","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Uthay, a man of Hamdan: We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with what were you sent - meaning the day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, in the Hajj. He said: I was sent with four: None enters Paradise except a believing soul, and none circumambulates the House naked, and whoever had between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a covenant, his covenant is to its term, and the polytheists and the Muslims do not perform Hajj after this year of theirs."
"595","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that debt is before bequest, while you recite bequest before debt, and that full brothers from the mother inherit to exclusion of half-brothers by the father."
"596","Sufyan narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will not give you and leave the people of the Suffah with their bellies twisting from hunger. And he said once: I will not employ you two and leave the people of the Suffah folding."
"597","Abu Abdurrahman Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatwani narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Harb Abu Sufyan al-Minqari informed me: Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Jafar narrated to us: My uncle narrated to me from his father that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening between al-Safa and al-Marwah in the course, uncovering his garment, it having reached to his knees."
"598","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to me: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seek permission. If he was in prayer he would glorify, and if he was not in prayer he would permit me."
"599","Sufyan narrated to us from Mutarrif from al-Shabi from Abu Juhayfah who said: We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Is there with you anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides the Quran? He said: No, by Him who splits the seed and creates the soul, except understanding Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives a man in the Quran, or what is in the scroll. I said: And what is in the scroll? He said: Blood money, freeing the captive, and a Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever."
"600","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr who said: Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed me: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi informed me - and he said once: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi informed him - that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, I and al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad, and said: Go until you come to Rawdat Khakh, for there is a woman traveler with her a letter, so take it from her. So we set out, our horses racing with us, until we came to the garden, and there we were with the woman traveler. We said: Bring out the letter. She said: I have no letter with me. We said: You will surely bring out the letter or we will overturn the clothes. He said: So she brought out the letter from her braids. So we took the letter and came with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in it was: From Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to some people of the polytheists at Makkah, informing them of some matter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hatib, what is this? He said: Do not hasten upon me. I was a man attached among Quraysh, and I was not of themselves, and those with you of the Emigrants had kinships protecting their families at Makkah, so I loved, since I lacked that of lineage among them, to take among them a favor by which they protect my kin, and I did not do that out of disbelief nor apostasy from my religion nor contentment with disbelief after Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has told you truth. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: He witnessed Badr, and what informs you? Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"601","Abdullah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Sha'ir narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam, that Abu Ja'far narrated to him, from his father, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me three things. He said, I do not know whether it was for him specifically or for people generally. He forbade me qassi garments, and mitharah saddle covers, and reciting while bowing."
"602","Abdullah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me, Umar ibn Yunus, meaning al-Yamami, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar al-Yamami, from al-Hasan ibn Zayd ibn Hasan, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, came forward, and he said, O Ali, these two are the masters of the old and the young among the people of Paradise after the prophets and messengers."
"603","Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from a man who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying, I wanted to propose to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for his daughter. I said, I have nothing, so how. Then I remembered his kinship and his care, so I proposed to him for her. He said, Do you have anything. I said, No. He said, Then where is your Hutami armor which I gave you on such and such day. He said, It is with me. He said, Then give it to her."
"604","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Fatimah came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking a servant, and he said, Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than that. You glorify Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-three times, and praise Allah thirty-three times, one of them thirty-four times."
"605","Abdullah narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to me, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abu Abdullah Maslamah al-Razi narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Bajali, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Allah loves the believing servant who is oft-tested and oft-repenting."
"606","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Mundhir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I was a man who emitted much pre-seminal fluid, and I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, because of the position of his daughter, so I ordered al-Miqdad and he asked him, and he said, He washes his private part and performs ablution."
"607","Abdullah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukarram al-Kufi narrated to me, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, both said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"608","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Miqsam narrated to us, al-Harith al-Ukli narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I had two visits with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by night and by day, and when I entered upon him while he was praying he would clear his throat. I came to him one night and he said, Do you know what the angel did tonight. I was praying and I heard a movement in the house, so I went out and there was Jibril, peace be upon him, and he said, I have been waiting for you all this night. There is a dog in your house, so I could not enter, and we do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor one who is in a state of major impurity, nor an image."
"609","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man al-Hamdani, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sacrificing an animal with a slit facing forward, or a slit facing backward, or a split ear, or a pierced ear, or a docked ear."
"610","Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, No prayer is performed after Asr unless the sun is white and high."
"611","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me to recite while bowing, and forbade gold rings, and qassi garments, and saffron-dyed garments."
"612","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said, Abu Musa came to al-Hasan ibn Ali to visit him in illness, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him, Have you come to visit or to gloat. He said, No, rather to visit. He said, Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him, If you have come to visit, then I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, When a man visits his Muslim brother, he walks in the harvest of Paradise until he sits, and when he sits mercy covers him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning."
"613","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us in the year two hundred and twenty-six, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said, I said to Suwayd, Why was he called al-Zanji. He said, He was intensely dark-skinned. From Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Rafi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at Arafah with Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, and said, This is a standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. Then he moved on, traveling at a gentle pace, while the people struck to the right and left, and he turned and said, Calmness, O people, calmness, O people, until he came to Muzdalifah and combined the two prayers. Then he stood at Muzdalifah and took al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him. Then he stood at Quzah and said, This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place. Then he moved on, traveling at a gentle pace, while the people struck to the right and left, and he turned and said, Calmness, O people, calmness, O people. When he stopped at Muhassir, he struck his mount and it trotted with him until it left the valley. Then he continued his journey until he came to the Jamarah. Then he entered the slaughter place and said, This is the slaughter place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Abdah, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman, the like of it or similar to it."
"614","Abdullah narrated to us, Ismail Abu Ma'mar narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayrah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, None hates the Arabs except a hypocrite."
"615","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said, Whoever claims that we have anything that we recite except the Book of Allah and this sheet, a sheet containing the ages of camels and matters of wounds, has lied. He said, And in it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Madinah is a sanctuary between Ayr and Thawr. Whoever introduces an innovation therein or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any obligatory or voluntary recompense. Whoever claims kinship to other than his father or allies himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary or obligatory recompense. And the protection of the Muslims is one, the lowest of them strives to uphold it."
"616","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, falling from the sky is dearer to me than lying about him. And when I narrate to you from others, I am but a man at war, and war is deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, There will emerge at the end of time a people young in age, foolish in minds, speaking from the speech of the best of creation. Their faith will not pass their throats. Wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for whoever kills them on the Day of Resurrection."
"617","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of the Confederates, They distracted us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer. May Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire. Then he prayed it between the two night prayers, between Maghrib and Isha."
"618","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Mundhir Abu Ya'la, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, He was a man who emitted much pre-seminal fluid, and he was shy to ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about pre-seminal fluid. He said, So he said to al-Miqdad, Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about pre-seminal fluid for me. He said, So he asked him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Therein is ablution."
"619","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to recite while bowing or prostrating."
"620","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, why do you choose carefully among Quraysh and leave us. He said, Do you have anything with you. He said, I said, Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. He said, She is not lawful for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling."
"621","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was one day sitting with a stick in his hand with which he was scratching. He said, Then he raised his head and said, There is none among you but his place in Paradise and in Hell is known. He said, They said, O Messenger of Allah, then why should we work. He said, Work, for each is facilitated for that for which he was created. As for whoever gives, fears Allah, and believes in the best, We shall facilitate for him ease. And as for whoever withholds, deems himself self-sufficient, and denies the best, We shall facilitate for him hardship."
"622","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment and appointed over them a man from the Ansar. He said, When they went out, he said, He held something against them, and said, He said to them, Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, command you to obey me. He said, They said, Yes. He said, Then he said, Gather firewood, then he called for fire and kindled it therein. Then he said, I adjure you to enter it. He said, The people were about to enter it. He said, Then a young man among them said to them, You only fled to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Fire, so do not hasten until you meet the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. If he commands you to enter it, then enter. He said, So they returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, and he said to them, Had you entered it, you would never have come out of it. Obedience is only in what is right."
"623","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Mu'adh narrated to me, who said, I attended a funeral among Banu Salimah and stood, and Nafi ibn Jubayr said to me, Sit, for I shall inform you about this with firm proof. Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam al-Zuraqi narrated to me that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, at the open square of Kufah saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to stand for funerals, then he sat after that and commanded us to sit."
"624","Ismail narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Abdullah al-Danaj, from Hudayn Abu Sasan al-Raqashi, that people from Kufah came to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him of what had happened concerning al-Walid, meaning his drinking wine. Ali spoke to him about that, and he said, Take your cousin and establish the legal punishment upon him. He said, O Hasan, stand and lash him. He said, You are not concerned with this in any way, entrust this to another. He said, Rather you have become weak, feeble, and incapable. Stand, O Abdullah ibn Ja'far. So Abdullah began to strike him while Ali counted, until he reached forty. Then he said, Stop. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lashed forty, and Abu Bakr forty, and Umar completed it to eighty, and each is a precedent."
"625","Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ubaydullah al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, Ali came into my house and called for ablution water. I brought him a cup holding a mudd or near it, until it was placed before him, and he had urinated. He said, O Ibn Abbas, shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said, Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said, A vessel was placed for him, and he washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth, sniffed water and blew it out. Then he took with his hands and struck his face with them, and placed his thumbs on what faces forward of his ears. He said, Then he repeated the like of that three times. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it upon his forelock, then let it flow upon his face. Then he washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then his other hand the like of that. Then he wiped his head and his ears, their outer sides. Then he took with his palms some water and struck with them upon his feet, with sandals upon them, then turned them over, then upon the other foot the like of that. He said, I said, Even with the sandals. He said, Even with the sandals. I said, Even with the sandals. He said, Even with the sandals. I said, Even with the sandals. He said, Even with the sandals."
"626","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Khawarij were mentioned, and he said, Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a small hand, or a malformed hand. Were it not that you would become boastful, I would have told you what Allah has promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad. I said, Did you hear it from Muhammad. He said, Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah."
"627","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach us the Quran so long as he was not in a state of major impurity."
"628","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, when you send me, shall I be like a heated plowshare, or shall the witness see what the absent does not see. He said, The witness sees what the absent does not see."
"629","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Mansur narrated to us, who said, I heard Rib'i, who said, I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."
"630","Husayn narrated it to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, who said, I heard Ali saying, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."
"631","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, We saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stand, so we stood, and sit, so we sat."
"632","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Ali ibn Mudrik narrated to me, from Abu Zur'ah, from Ibn Nujayy, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Angels do not enter a house in which there is one in major impurity, nor an image, nor a dog."
"633","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or ear."
"634","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourd vessels and pitched vessels. Abu Abd al-Rahman said, I heard my father saying, There is no hadith in Kufah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, more authentic than this."
"635","Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, Amir narrated to me, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed ten: the eater of usury, its feeder, its scribe, its two witnesses, the one who marries to make lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful, the withholder of charity, the tattooer and the one tattooed."
"636","Yahya narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen while I was young in age. He said, I said, You send me to a people among whom disputes occur, while I have no knowledge of judging. He said, Allah will guide your tongue and steady your heart. He said, I never doubted in judging between two after that."
"637","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was in pain, and I was saying, O Allah, if my term has come, then relieve me, and if it is distant, then raise me, and if it is a trial, then make me patient. He said, What did you say. So I repeated it to him, and he struck me with his foot and said, What did you say. He said, So I repeated it to him, and he said, O Allah, grant him health, or heal him. He said, I never complained of that pain after that."
"638","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said, I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I was ill, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said, O Allah, grant him health, O Allah, heal him. So I never complained of that pain after that."
"639","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, who said, I came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, I and two men, and he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would relieve himself, then go out and recite the Quran, and eat meat with us. Nothing barred him from the Quran except major impurity, and perhaps he said, veiled him."
"640","He said, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, The best of its women is Maryam daughter of Imran, and the best of its women is Khadijah."
"641","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim al-Kindi, from Zadhan Abu Umar, who said, I heard Ali at al-Rahbah adjuring the people, Who witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Ghadir Khumm saying what he said. So thirteen men stood and testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master."
"642","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, By Allah, it is among what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to me, that none hates me except a hypocrite, and none loves me except a believer."
"643","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Za'idah informed us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prepared Fatimah with a velvet cloth, a waterskin, and a leather pillow stuffed with idhkhir fiber."
"644","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hakim al-Mada'ini narrated to us, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I set out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until we came to the Ka'bah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me, Sit, and he climbed upon my shoulders. I went to rise with him, but he saw weakness in me, so he descended, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat for me and said, Climb upon my shoulders. He said, So I climbed upon his shoulders. He said, Then he rose with me. He said, It seemed to me that had I wished I could have reached the horizon of the sky, until I climbed upon the House, and upon it was an idol of brass or copper. I began to wrestle it from its right, its left, before it, and behind it, until when I had mastered it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me, Throw it down. So I threw it down and it shattered as glass vessels shatter. Then I descended, and I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out racing until we were hidden by houses, fearing that anyone among the people would meet us."
"645","Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Yasin al-Ijli narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, The Mahdi is from us, the people of the House. Allah will rectify him in a night."
"646","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, judge of Rayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said, I heard Amir al-Mu'minin Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying, I gathered with Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, al-Abbas, and Zayd ibn Harithah at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Al-Abbas said, O Messenger of Allah, my age has grown, my bones have thinned, and my expenses have multiplied. If you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, to order for me so many wasqs of food, then do so. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, We shall do so. Fatimah said, O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to order for me as you ordered for your uncle, then do so. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, We shall do that. Then Zayd ibn Harithah said, O Messenger of Allah, you had given me land from which my livelihood came, then you took it back. If you see fit to return it to me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, We shall do so. Fatimah said, O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to order for me as you ordered for your uncle, then do so. The Messenger of Allah said, We shall do that. He said, Then I said, O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to entrust to me this right which Allah has placed for us in His Book from this fifth, so that I distribute it in your lifetime lest anyone dispute me over it after you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, We shall do that. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime, until the last year of the years of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when much wealth came to him."
"647","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Sharhabil ibn Mudrik al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy al-Hadrami, from his father, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me, I had a position with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that none of creation had. I would come to him every dawn and greet him until he cleared his throat. One night I came and greeted him, saying, Peace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah. He said, Wait, O Abu Hasan, until I come out to you. When he came out to me, I said, O Prophet of Allah, has anyone angered you. He said, No. I said, Then why do you not speak to me as before, until you spoke to me tonight. He said, I heard a movement in the chamber, and said, Who is this. He said, I am Jibril. I said, Enter. He said, No, come out to me. When I went out, he said, In your house is something into which no angel enters so long as it is therein. I said, I know of none, O Jibril. He said, Go and look. So I opened the house and found nothing therein except a puppy with which al-Hasan was playing. I said, I found only a puppy. He said, They are three into which no angel will ever enter so long as therein: a dog, or major impurity, or an image of a living soul."
"648","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Sharhabil ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, that he traveled with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and was the keeper of his ablution water. When he came opposite Nineveh while heading to Siffin, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, called out, Be patient, Abu Abdullah, be patient, Abu Abdullah, at the shore of the Euphrates. I said, What is that. He said, I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day while his eyes were flowing. I said, O Prophet of Allah, has anyone angered you. What is the matter with your eyes flowing. He said, Rather Jibril had just stood from with me and told me that al-Husayn will be killed at the shore of the Euphrates. He said, Then he said, Do you wish that I make you smell some of its soil. He said, I said, Yes. So he stretched his hand, took a handful of dust, and gave it to me, and I could not hold back my eyes from flowing."
"649","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, al-Azhar ibn Rashid al-Kahili informed us, from al-Khidr ibn al-Qawwas, from Abu Sukhaylah, who said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Shall I not inform you of the best verse in the Book of Allah Almighty, which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us. Whatever misfortune befalls you is from what your hands have earned, and He pardons much. And I shall explain it to you, O Ali. Whatever befalls you of illness, punishment, or trial in this world is from what your hands have earned, and Allah Almighty is nobler than to repeat the punishment upon them in the Hereafter. And whatever Allah Almighty has pardoned in this world, Allah Almighty is more forbearing than to return after His pardon."
"650","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan, Isra'il, and my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, who said, We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the voluntary prayers of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by day. He said, You cannot bear it. He said, We said, Inform us of it, we shall take from it what we can. He said, When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr, he waited until the sun was from here, meaning from the east, at the measure of the Asr prayer from here, from the west, then he stood and prayed two units. Then he waited until the sun was from here, meaning from the east, at the measure of the Zuhr prayer from here, meaning from the west, then he stood and prayed four, and four before Zuhr when the sun declined, and two after it, and four before Asr, separating between every two units with salutations upon the close angels, the prophets, and those among the believers and Muslims who follow them. He said, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Those are sixteen units, the voluntary prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by day, and few persist in them. Waki narrated to us, from his father, who said, Habib ibn Abi Thabit said to Abu Ishaq when he narrated it, O Abu Ishaq, this hadith of yours equals your mosque filled with gold."
"651","Aswad ibn Amir and Husayn said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed witr at every part of the night, its beginning, its middle, and its end, then witr became established at the end of the night."
"652","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, Witr is not obligatory like prayer, but it is a practice which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, established."
"653","Waki narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed witr at the beginning of the night, its end, and its middle, then his witr ended at dawn."
"654","Waki narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I saw us on the day of Badr seeking shelter with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was the closest of us to the enemy, and he was among the strongest of people that day in valor."
"655","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim al-Hanafi narrated to us, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, O Messenger of Allah, we are in the desert, and wind exits from one of us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Allah Almighty is not shy of the truth. When one of you does that, let him perform ablution, and do not approach women in their posteriors. And he said once, In their anuses."
"656","Ishaq ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Amr al-Qari, who said, Abdullah ibn Shaddad came and entered upon A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, while we were sitting with her, on his return from Iraq in the nights when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed. She said to him, O Abdullah ibn Shaddad, will you tell me truthfully about what I ask you, and narrate to me about those people whom Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, killed. He said, Why should I not tell you truthfully. She said, Then narrate to me their story. He said, When Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, corresponded with Mu'awiyah and the two arbiters arbitrated, eight thousand among the reciters of the people went out against him and camped in a land called Harura on the side of Kufah. They blamed him, saying, You have shed a shirt which Allah Almighty clothed you with, and a name which Allah Almighty named you with, then you went and appointed arbiters in the religion of Allah, yet judgment belongs only to Allah Almighty. When what they blamed him for and their parting from him over it reached Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he ordered a caller to call that none should enter upon Amir al-Mu'minin except a man who carries the Quran. When the house filled with reciters of the people, he called for a great master copy of the Quran, placed it before him, and began to strike it with his hand, saying, O Quran, speak to the people. The people called to him, saying, O Amir al-Mu'minin, what are you asking of it. It is but ink upon paper, and we speak of what we have memorized from it, so what do you want. He said, Your companions, those who went out, between me and them is the Book of Allah. Allah Almighty says in His Book concerning a woman and a man, If you fear a breach between them, send an arbiter from his folk and an arbiter from her folk. If they desire reconciliation, Allah will bring agreement between them. So the community of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is greater in blood and sanctity than a woman and a man. They blamed me for corresponding with Mu'awiyah, writing, Ali ibn Abi Talib. And Suhayl ibn Amr had come to us while we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hudaybiyah, when he made peace with his people Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote, In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Suhayl said, Do not write, In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. He said, How shall we write. He said, Write, In Your name, O Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Write, Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. He said, Had I known you are the Messenger of Allah, I would not have opposed you. So he wrote, This is what Muhammad ibn Abdullah has made peace upon with Quraysh. Allah Almighty says in His Book, You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example for whoever hopes in Allah and the Last Day. Then Ali sent to them Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and I went out with him, until when we reached the midst of their camp, Ibn al-Kawwa stood addressing the people, saying, O bearers of the Quran, this is Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Whoever does not know him, I shall make him known from the Book of Allah by what he is known by. This is among those concerning whom and his people it was revealed, A quarrelsome people. So return him to his companion and do not present to him the Book of Allah. Their speakers stood and said, By Allah, we shall present to him the Book of Allah. If he brings truth we recognize, we shall follow him, and if he brings falsehood, we shall refute him with his falsehood. So they presented to Abdullah the Book for three days, and four thousand among them returned, all repentant, among them Ibn al-Kawwa, until he brought them to Ali in Kufah. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to the remainder, saying, What has happened of our affair and the affair of the people you have seen, so stand where you wish until the community of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gathers, on condition between us and you that you shed no unlawful blood, nor cut a road, nor wrong a protected person. For if you do, we have cast war to you on equal terms. Allah does not love the treacherous. A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said to him, O Ibn Shaddad, yet he killed them. He said, By Allah, he did not send against them until they cut roads, shed blood, and violated protected people. She said, By Allah. He said, By Allah besides Whom there is no god, it was so. She said, What is this thing reported to me from protected people speaking of, saying, The one with the nipple, the one with the nipple. He said, I saw him, and I stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, over him among the slain. He called the people and said, Do you know this. How many came saying, I saw him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so praying, and I saw him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so praying, yet they brought no firm proof by which he was known except that. She said, What did Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say when he stood over him, as the people of Iraq claim. He said, I heard him saying, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truthfully. She said, Did you hear him say other than that. He said, O Allah, no. She said, Yes, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truthfully. May Allah have mercy upon Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. It was among his speech that he saw nothing pleasing him but he said, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truthfully. So the people of Iraq go and lie about him and add to the hadith."
"657","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Abu Muhammad al-Hudhali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at a funeral and said, Which of you will go to Madinah and leave therein no idol but he breaks it, nor a grave but he levels it, nor an image but he defaces it. A man said, I, O Messenger of Allah. So he went, but he feared the people of Madinah and returned. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I shall go, O Messenger of Allah. He said, Go. So he went, then returned and said, O Messenger of Allah, I left therein no idol but I broke it, nor a grave but I leveled it, nor an image but I defaced it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Whoever returns to making anything of this has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said, Do not be a troublemaker, nor arrogant, nor a trader except a trader of good, for those are outstripped by deeds."
"658","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from a man among the people of Basrah, whom the people of Basrah nickname Abu Muwarri, and the people of Kufah nickname him Abu Muhammad, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at a funeral, and he mentioned the hadith, but he did not say, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said, Nor an image but he obliterates it. Then he said, I did not come to you, O Messenger of Allah, until I left no image but I obliterated it. And he said, Do not be a troublemaker, nor arrogant."
"659","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, He used to pray witr at the call to prayer and pray two units at the establishment of prayer."
"660","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Ja'far, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from a man among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, There is no doubt except that it is Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of usury, its feeder, its two witnesses, its scribe, the tattooer and the one tattooed, the one who marries to make lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful, the withholder of charity, and he used to forbid wailing."
"661","Khalaf narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Zabyan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, O Ali, if you are entrusted with rule after me, then expel the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula."
"662","Khalaf narrated to us, Abu Ja'far, meaning al-Razi, and Khalid, meaning al-Tahhan, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I was a man who emitted much pre-seminal fluid, so I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said, As for semen, therein is washing, and as for pre-seminal fluid, therein is ablution."
"663","Khalaf narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to raise his voice with recitation before Isha and after it, confusing his companions while they prayed."
"664","Khalaf narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Ask Allah Almighty for guidance and uprightness, and recall with guidance your guiding the road, and recall with uprightness your straightening the arrow."
"665","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us. Abdullah said, And I heard it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah. Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Kathir al-Nawwa, from Abdullah ibn Mulayl, who said, I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, There is no prophet before me but he was given seven leaders, ministers, nobles, and I have been given fourteen ministers, leaders, nobles, seven from Quraysh and seven from the Emigrants."
"666","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and I said, O Messenger of Allah, you send me to a people older than me to judge among them. He said, Go, for Allah Almighty will steady your tongue and guide your heart."
"667","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us, Amr ibn Ghuzayy narrated to me, my uncle Ilba narrated to me, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, Charity camels passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said, He reached with his hand to a tuft of hair on the side of a camel and said, I am no more entitled to this tuft than any man among the Muslims."
"668","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying, he left while we were standing. Then he came forward with his head dripping, and prayed the prayer for us. Then he said, I remembered that I was in major impurity when I stood for prayer and had not washed. So whoever among you finds rumbling in his belly, or is in the like of what I was in, let him leave until he attends to his need or his washing, then return to his prayer."
"669","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"670","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Rabi, meaning Ibn Abi Salih al-Aslami, narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, adjuring the people, saying, I adjure by Allah a Muslim man who heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm what he said. So twelve men who fought at Badr stood and testified."
"671","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the companion of usury, its eater, its scribe, its two witnesses, the one who marries to make lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful."
"672","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Kathir, freedman of the Ansar, narrated to us, who said, I was with my master Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, where the people of Nahrawan were killed, and the people felt unease in themselves over their killing. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, O people, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has told us of peoples who exit the religion as the arrow exits the game, then never return to it ever, until the arrow returns to its notch. And the sign of that is that among them is a black man with a defective hand, one of his hands like the breast of a woman, with a nipple like the nipple of a woman's breast, around it seven hairs. So seek him, for I see him among them. So they sought him and found him at the edge of the river beneath the slain. They brought him out, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, magnified Allah, saying, Allah is Greatest, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truthfully. He was wearing an Arab bow of his, so he took it in his hand and began to pierce his defective limb with it, saying, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truthfully. The people magnified Allah when they saw him and rejoiced, and what they had felt left them."
"673","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, For a Muslim upon a Muslim are six acts of kindness: he greets him when he meets him, he blesses him when he sneezes, he visits him when ill, he answers him when he invites him, he attends him when he dies, he loves for him what he loves for himself, and he advises him in absence."
"674","Husayn narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, and he mentioned similar to it with its chain and meaning."
"675","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, The Hour will not come until a man among my companions is sought as a stray is sought, and is not found."
"676","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Badr, Whomever you are able to capture among Banu Abd al-Muttalib, for they came out under compulsion."
"677","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, And you make your provision that you deny. He said, Your associating: We were rained by such and such star, by such and such star."
"678","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and Aswad ibn Amir said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with nine chapters of the Mufassal. Aswad said, He recites in the first unit, Rivalry diverted you, We sent it down in the Night of Decree, and When the earth is shaken, and in the second unit, By time, When the help of Allah comes, and We have given you al-Kawthar, and in the third unit, Say, O disbelievers, Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"679","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, I heard Abd al-A'la narrating, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that a slave girl of theirs committed adultery and became pregnant. Ali came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, and he said to him, Leave her until she gives birth, then lash her."
"680","Hashim and Hasan said, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said, Ibn Jurmuz sought permission from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said, Who is this. They said, Ibn Jurmuz seeks permission. He said, Permit him to enter. The killer of al-Zubayr is in the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"681","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said, Ibn Jurmuz sought permission from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, while I was with him. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Give the killer of Ibn Safiyyah tidings of the Fire. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr. I heard Sufyan saying, The disciple is the supporter."
"682","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, who heard Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Duha."
"683","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Jarir ibn Hayyan, from his father, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I send you with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me. He commanded me to level every grave and obliterate every idol."
"684","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was large-headed, great-eyed, long-lashed, his eyes tinged with redness, thick-bearded, luminous in color. When he walked he leaned forward as though walking uphill, and when he turned he turned wholly, coarse in palms and feet."
"685","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to me, Abu Bakr informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three units."
"686","Aswad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited after passing wind, before touching water. And perhaps Isra'il said, from a man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"687","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Musa al-Saghir al-Tahhan, from Mujahid, who said, Ali said, I went out and came to a garden. He said, A bucket for a date. He said, So I drew water until I filled my palm, then I came to water and made it sweet, meaning I drank. Then I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and fed him some of it, and I ate some of it."
"688","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, I have vowed to slaughter my she-camel, and such and such. He said, As for your she-camel, slaughter it, and as for such and such, it is from Satan."
"689","Abu Nuh, meaning Qurrad, narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu al-Tayyah, I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrating, from a man from Banu Asad, who said, Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came out to us, and they asked him about witr. He said, Then he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to pray witr at this hour. Call out, O Ibn al-Nabbah, or give the call, or the establishment."
"690","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me, When two litigants come to you, do not hear the speech of the first until you hear the speech of the other. Then you will see how to judge. He said, Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I never ceased to be a judge after that."
"691","Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Sallam Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zabyan, from Hukaym ibn Sa'd Abu Tihya, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intended travel, he said, O Allah, by You I attack, by You I roam, and by You I travel."
"692","Abu al-Nadr Hashim and Abu Dawud said, Warqa narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped, and he ordered me to give the cupper his wage."
"693","Bakr ibn Isa al-Rasibi narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to bring him a dish in which he would write what his community would not stray from after him. He said, I feared his soul would pass before that. He said, I said, I memorize and retain. He said, Enjoin prayer, alms, and what your right hands possess."
"694","Hujayn narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, Whoever lies about me in his dream will be burdened with tying a grain of barley on the Day of Resurrection."
"695","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Fudayl ibn Sulayman, meaning al-Numayri, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Amr al-Aslami, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, After me there will be disagreement or a matter. If you are able to be peace, then do so."
"696","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warakani, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to me, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us. They said, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, Allah Almighty named war upon the tongue of His Prophet as deception. Rahmawayh said in his hadith, Upon the tongue of your Prophet."
"697","Abdullah narrated to us, my father and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me. They said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan, one who heard Ali narrated to me, saying, War is deception upon the tongue of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"698","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, who heard Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was gifted a striped silk robe, and he sent it to me. So I went with it, and I recognized anger in the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said, So I divided it among my women."
"699","Abdullah ibn al-Walid and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, Sufyan said, I do not know but that he raised it. Whoever lies in his dream will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection with tying a grain of barley. Abu Ahmad said, I deem it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"700","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to continue fasting until dawn."
"701","Rawh narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me, when distress befalls me, to say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous, glory be to Allah, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and all praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"702","Ubaidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah narrated to me, from his father, he said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari visited al-Hasan ibn Ali. He said: Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, entered and said: Did you come, O Abu Musa, as one visiting the sick or as a visitor? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, rather as one visiting the sick. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim visits a Muslim except seventy thousand angels invoke blessings upon him from the time of morning until he enters evening, and Allah the Exalted assigns for him a Kharif in Paradise. He said: So we said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is Kharif? He said: The water channel that irrigates the palm trees."
"703","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, Sharik informed us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zar'ah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came to a people of Basra from the Khawarij, among them a man called al-Ja'd ibn Ba'jah. He said to him: Fear Allah, O Ali, for you are going to die. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Rather I shall be killed; a blow upon this that will dye this, meaning his beard, from his head; a covenanted covenant and a decreed decree, and he has failed who invents falsehood. And he criticized him about his clothing, so he said: What have you to do with clothing? It is farther from arrogance and more fitting for the Muslim to follow my example."
"704","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi mentioned, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-A'war, he said: I said: I shall surely go to the Commander of the Faithful and ask him about what I heard in the evening. He said: So I came to him after the night prayer and entered upon him, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: O Muhammad, your community will differ after you. He said: So I said to him: Where is the way out, O Jibril? He said: So he said: The Book of Allah the Exalted, by it Allah breaks every tyrant; whoever clings to it is saved, and whoever abandons it perishes, twice; a decisive word, and it is not jest; tongues do not wear it out, and its wonders do not end; in it is the news of what was before you, and the judgment between you, and the report of what will be after you."
"705","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Shihab, from Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and upon Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, at night and woke us for prayer. He said: Then he returned to his house and prayed a good while of the night. He said: Then he did not hear any sound from us. He said: So he returned to us and woke us and said: Stand and pray. He said: So I sat while rubbing my eyes and saying: By Allah, we only pray what has been written for us; our souls are in the Hand of Allah, and if He wills to send us He sends us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away saying, while striking his hand upon his thigh: We only pray what has been written for us, we only pray what has been written for us; and man is the most argumentative of things."
"706","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jamil Abu Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyyah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: When the Khawarij rebelled at al-Nahrawan, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood among his companions and said: These people have shed sacred blood and raided the pastures of the people, and they are the nearest enemy to you; if you march to your enemy I fear these will succeed you among those behind you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A faction will emerge from my community; your prayer is nothing compared to their prayer, nor your fasting compared to their fasting, nor your recitation compared to their recitation; they recite the Qur'an thinking it is for them while it is against them; it does not pass their throats; they pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the prey; and the sign of that is that among them is a man with an upper arm but no forearm, upon it like a nipple of a breast, upon it white hairs. If the army that strikes them knew what is theirs upon the tongue of their Prophet, they would rely upon deeds. So march in the name of Allah. Then he mentioned the hadith at length."
"707","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: By Allah, we were with Uthman ibn Affan at al-Juhfah, and with him a group of the people of Syria, among them Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, when Uthman said, and tamattu' of Umrah to Hajj was mentioned to him: The most complete for Hajj and Umrah is that they not be in the months of Hajj; if you delayed this Umrah until you visit this House twice it would be better, for Allah the Exalted has widened goodness; while Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, was in the belly of the valley feeding a camel of his. He said: What Uthman said reached him, so he came until he stood over Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Did you deliberately go to a practice practiced by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a concession Allah the Exalted granted to the servants in His Book, to restrict them therein and forbid it, though it was for one in need and one far from home? Then he entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together. Then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, turned to the people and said: Did I forbid it? I did not forbid it; it was only an opinion I advised; whoever wishes takes it and whoever wishes leaves it."
"708","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, then al-Zuraqi, from his mother, that she narrated to him, she said: As if I am looking at Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was upon the white mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at the pass of the Ansar during the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: These are not days of fasting; they are only days of eating and drinking and remembrance."
"709","Ya'qub and Sa'd said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, Sa'd said: Ibn al-Had, I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I never heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine his father and mother for anyone other than Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, for I heard him say on the day of Uhud: Shoot, O Sa'd, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"710","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me, I do not say he forbade you, gold rings, and wearing Qassi and saffron-dyed garments, and reciting the Qur'an while bowing; and he clothed me in a garment of Sira' silk, so I went out in it, and he said: O Ali, I did not clothe you in it for you to wear it. He said: So I returned with it to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, and gave her its edge, and she took it to fold it up with me, so I split it in two. He said: So she said: May your hands be covered in dust, O son of Abu Talib, what have you done? He said: So I said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me its wearing, so wear it and clothe your women in it."
"711","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have exempted you from horses and slaves, so give the charity of silver, from every forty dirhams a dirham; and there is nothing due in ninety and one hundred; and when it reaches two hundred, in it are five dirhams."
"712","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you words, when you say them you will be forgiven, although you are forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Mighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne; all praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"713","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zabyan, from Abu Tihya, he said: When Ibn Muljam struck Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the blow, Ali said: Do with him as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to do with a man who intended to kill him, and he said: Kill him, then burn him."
"714","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Nu'aym ibn Dijajah, that he said: Abu Mas'ud Uqbah ibn Amr al-Ansari entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Ali said to him: Are you the one who says: There will not come upon people one hundred years while upon the earth an eye blinks? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: There will not come upon people one hundred years while upon the earth an eye blinks, of those alive today. By Allah, the hope of this community is after one hundred years."
"715","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr and Abu Sa'id said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, with a velvet cloth, a waterskin, and a pillow of leather stuffed with idhkhir. Abu Sa'id said: Fibre."
"716","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah, and al-Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, that they heard him narrate that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he stoned the woman of Kufa, flogged her on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and said: I flog her by the Book of Allah and stone her by the practice of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"717","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Fulan ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib al-Hashimi, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he stood for the prescribed prayer he said takbir and raised his hands level with his shoulders, and did likewise when he finished his recitation and intended to bow, and did so when he raised his head from bowing, and he did not raise his hands in any part of his prayer while sitting; and when he rose from the two prostrations he raised his hands likewise and said takbir."
"718","Ali ibn Hafs informed us, Warqa' informed us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal, from Nu'aym ibn Dijajah, he said: Abu Mas'ud entered upon Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Are you the one who says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will not come upon people one hundred years while upon the earth a breathing soul remains? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: There will not come upon people one hundred years while upon the earth a breathing soul remains, of those alive today; and the hope of this community is after the hundred."
"719","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ata' al-Khurasani, that he narrated to him, from the freedman of his wife, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When it is Friday, the devils go out keeping people back to their markets, with banners with them, and the angels sit at the doors of the mosques recording people according to their ranks: the foremost, and the praying one, and the one next to him, until the imam comes out. Whoever is near the imam and listens attentively or hears and does not engage in idle talk will have two shares of reward; and whoever is far from him and hears and listens attentively and does not engage in idle talk will have one share of reward; and whoever is near the imam and engages in idle talk and does not listen attentively nor hear will have two shares of burden; and whoever is far from him and engages in idle talk and does not listen attentively nor hear will have one share of burden; and whoever says: Be quiet, has spoken; and whoever speaks, there is no Friday for him. Then he said: Thus I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"720","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a man from my companions is sought as a stray camel is sought, and is not found."
"721","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who writes usury, the one who consumes it, its two witnesses, the one who marries a woman to make her lawful for her former husband, and the one for whom that is done."
"722","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard Hubayrah say: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me, gold rings, and Qassi garments, and Mitharah saddles."
"723","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The mukatab is ransomed in proportion to what he has paid."
"724","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zubayd al-Iyami, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and appointed a man over them; so he lit a fire and said: Enter it. Some people intended to enter it, and others said: We only fled from it. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to those who intended to enter it: Had you entered it you would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection; and he said to the others a good word; and said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah; obedience is only in what is right."
"725","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, I heard al-A'mash narrate, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the people: What do you think about surplus remaining with us of this wealth? The people said: O Commander of the Faithful, we have kept you from your family, your property and your trade, so it is yours. He said to me: What do you say? I said: They have advised you. He said to me: Speak. I said: Why make your certainty conjecture? He said: You shall surely explain what you said. I said: Yes, by Allah, I shall surely explain it. Do you remember when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you as a collector, and you came to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, and he withheld his charity from you, and there was something between you, and you said to me: Come with me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We found him troubled, so we returned; then we came to him in the morning and found him cheerful. You informed him of what he had done, and he said to you: Do you not know that the paternal uncle of a man is like his father? And we mentioned to him what we had seen of his troubled state on the first day and what we had seen of his cheerfulness on the second day, and he said: You came to me on the first day while two dinars of charity remained with me, so what you saw of my troubled state was due to that; and you came to me today after I had sent them forth, so that is what you saw of my cheerfulness. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You have spoken truthfully; by Allah, I shall thank you for the first and the last."
"726","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me these words and commanded me, if distress or hardship befalls me, to say them: There is no god but Allah, the Generous, the Forbearing, glory be to Him; and blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; and all praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"727","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zad han, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a spot of a hair of major impurity untouched by water, Allah the Exalted will do such and such to him of the Fire. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: From then I became hostile to my hair."
"728","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in seven garments."
"729","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Majishun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Fadl and al-Majishun narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Ubaydullah ibn Rafi', from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said takbir, began then said: I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, upright, submitting, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer, my sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, with no partner for Him; and with that I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims. Abu al-Nadr said: And I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, there is no god but You; You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I have wronged myself and acknowledged my sin, so forgive me all my sins; none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of morals; none guides to the best of them but You; and turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil from me but You. Blessed are You and Exalted; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. And when he bowed he said: O Allah, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, to You I have submitted; my hearing, my sight, my brain, my bones and my nerves are humbled to You. And when he raised his head from the bow he said: Allah hears him who praises Him; our Lord, and to You is praise, filling the heavens and the earth and what is between them, and filling what You will of anything after. And when he prostrated he said: O Allah, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, to You I have submitted; my face has prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and made its form excellent, and opened its hearing and sight; so blessed is Allah, the Best of creators. Then when he finished the prayer he said: O Allah, forgive me what I have sent forth and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have declared, and what I have transgressed, and what You know better than I; You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You."
"730","Waki' narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from al-Mundhir, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a son is born to me after you, shall I name him by your name and give him your kunyah? He said: Yes. So it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Ali."
"731","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged to me that none loves you but a believer, and none hates you but a hypocrite."
"732","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from Hujayyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear of the sacrificial animal."
"733","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim al-Batin, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: We were traveling with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, when a man was calling talbiyah for both together. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Who is this? They said: Ali. He said: Did you not know that I forbade this? He said: Yes, but I would not abandon the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for your word."
"734","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah, he said: A man asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the cow as sacrifice. He said: For seven. He said: With broken horn? He said: It does not harm you. He said: Lame? He said: When it reaches the place of sacrifice, slaughter it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear."
"735","Waki' narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim and Abu Amr ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, they heard it, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will emerge among whom is a man with a small hand, or a defective hand, or a deformed hand; and were it not that you would become overconfident I would inform you of what Allah has promised those who kill them upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abidah said: I said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah."
"736","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah al-Tuhawi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that a servant woman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed an offense, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to carry out the penalty upon her. I came to her and found her blood not yet dried. I came to him and informed him, and he said: When her blood has dried, carry out the penalty upon her. Carry out the penalties upon those your right hands possess."
"737","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I used to think the inner soles were more deserving of wiping than their outer sides, until I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping their outer sides."
"738","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman al-Thaqafi, may Allah be pleased with him, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to mate a donkey with a horse."
"739","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I appointed anyone as successor without consultation, I would have appointed Ibn Umm Abd."
"740","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, Ali narrated to us that Fatimah complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the effect of dough on her hands; some captives came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she came to him asking for a servant but did not find him, so she returned. He said: Then he came to us after we had taken our beds. He said: So I went to stand, and he said: Stay in your places. He came until he sat, until I felt the coolness of his feet. He said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than a servant? When you take your beds, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times."
"741","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu al-Hayyaj al-Asadi, he said: Ali said to me: I send you upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me: Leave no image except you efface it, and no elevated grave except you level it."
"742","Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love this chapter: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High."
"743","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Three men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One said: O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred dinars and gave ten dinars in charity from them. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I had ten dinars and gave a dinar in charity from them. Another said: I had a dinar and gave a tenth of it in charity. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are equal in reward; each of you gave a tenth of his wealth in charity."
"744","Waki' narrated to us, al-Mas'udi and Mis'ar narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had thick hands and feet and large joints."
"745","Waki' narrated to us, from Sharik, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two litigants sit with you, do not speak until you hear from the other as you heard from the first."
"746","Waki' informed us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither tall nor short, large of head and beard, thick of hands and feet, his face tinged with redness, long of the Masrubah, large of joints; when he walked he leaned forward as if descending a slope; I never saw before him nor after him one like him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"747","Yazid narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Khosrau gave a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he accepted from him; and Caesar gave him a gift and he accepted from him; and kings gave him gifts and he accepted from them."
"748","Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani', he said: I asked A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about wiping over the leather socks, and she said: Ask Ali, for he knows more about this than I; he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"749","Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"750","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in his right hand and silk in his left, then raised them with his hands and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my community."
"751","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Hisham ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and seek refuge in You from You; I cannot count praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"752","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade people raising voices over one another between Maghrib and Isha with the Qur'an."
"753","Yazid informed us, Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, brought a mount to ride; when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: In the name of Allah. When he sat upon it he said: All praise is due to Allah; glory be to the One who subjected this for us, and we were not capable of it; and to our Lord we shall surely return. Then he praised Allah three times and said takbir three times, then said: Glory be to You, there is no god but You; I have wronged myself, so forgive me. Then he laughed. I said: What are you laughing at, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as I did, then laugh. I said: What are you laughing at, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Lord marvels at His servant when he says: My Lord, forgive me, and says: My servant knows that none forgives sins but I."
"754","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata', from Abdullah ibn Yasar, that Amr ibn Hurayth visited al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Ali said to him: Do you visit al-Hasan while in your soul is what is in it? Amr said to him: You are not my Lord to turn my heart as you will. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: That does not prevent us from giving you counsel. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim visits his brother except Allah sends forth for him seventy thousand angels invoking blessings upon him, from whatever hours of day it is until he enters evening, and from whatever hours of night it is until he enters morning. Amr said to him: What do you say about walking with the funeral, in front of it or behind it? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The excellence of walking behind it over in front of it is like the excellence of the prescribed prayer in congregation over alone. Amr said: I saw Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, walking before the funeral. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: They only disliked inconveniencing the people."
"755","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me in a Sira' silk garment; I went out in it and saw anger in his face. He said: So I split it among my women."
"756","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, used to forbid tamattu', and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to command it. Uthman said to Ali: You are such and such. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You knew that we performed tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, but we were fearful."
"757","Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the infant: The urine of the boy is sprinkled, and the urine of the girl is washed. Qatadah said: And this is while they have not eaten food; when they eat, both are washed."
"758","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No servant believes until he believes in four: until he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah sent with the truth, and until he believes in resurrection after death, and until he believes in decree."
"759","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Najiyah ibn Ka'b narrate, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abu Talib has died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and bury him. He said: He died a polytheist. He said: Go and bury him. He said: When I had buried him I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Wash."
"760","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to sell two brother slaves; I sold them and separated them. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Catch them and return them, and do not sell them except together."
"761","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Witr is not obligatory like the prayer, but a practice practiced by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"762","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan and Shu'bah and Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten of Ramadan."
"763","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given what no one of the prophets was given. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it? He said: I have been aided by terror, given the keys of the earth, named Ahmad, the dust has been made purification for me, and my community has been made the best of communities."
"764","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr at the call to prayer and pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr at the iqamah."
"765","Abu al-Nadr informed us, al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Shayban, from Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We mentioned the Dajjal with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sleeping, and he woke with his color reddened, and said: Other than that is more fearful for me for you; he mentioned a word."
"766","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zar'ah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A mule was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a gift. I said: What is this? He said: A mule. I said: From what is it? He said: A donkey is mated with a horse, and this comes forth between them. I said: Shall we not mate such with such? He said: No; only those who do not know do that."
"767","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When I sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if he was in prayer he glorified Allah, and if otherwise he gave permission."
"768","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the place of sacrifice at Mina and said: This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice."
"769","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When al-Hasan was born I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? He said: I said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Hasan. When al-Husayn was born I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? He said: I said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Husayn. When the third was born I named him Harb. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them by the names of the sons of Harun: Shabbar, Shabbir and Mushabbir."
"770","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani' and Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When we left Mecca, the daughter of Hamzah followed us calling: O uncle, O uncle. He said: So I took her by her hand and handed her to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, and said: Take the daughter of your cousin. He said: When we reached Medina, we disputed about her, I and Ja'far and Zayd ibn Harithah. Ja'far said: The daughter of my uncle, and her maternal aunt is with me, meaning Asma' bint Umays. Zayd said: The daughter of my brother. I said: I took her, and she is the daughter of my uncle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Ja'far, you resemble my appearance and character; and as for you, O Ali, you are from me and I am from you; and as for you, O Zayd, you are our brother and our freedman; and the girl is with her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is a mother. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry her? He said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"771","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists. I said: Does a man seek forgiveness for his parents while they are polytheists? He said: Did not Ibrahim seek forgiveness for his father? I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so it was revealed: It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, up to His word: He dissociated from him. He said: When he died; I do not know whether Sufyan said it or Isra'il said it or it is in the hadith: When he died."
"772","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, my uncle Iyas ibn Amir narrated to me, I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while A'ishah lay between him and the qiblah."
"773","Hajjaj and Abu Nu'aym said: Fitr narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Abu al-Tufayl, Hajjaj said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there remained of the world but one day, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would send a man from us to fill it with justice as it was filled with injustice. Abu Nu'aym said: A man from us. He said: And I heard him once mention it, from Habib, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"774","Hajjaj narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Al-Hasan most resembles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between the chest and the head, and al-Husayn most resembles the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what is below that."
"775","Hajjaj said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah is more just than to repeat His punishment upon His servant; and whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals it and pardons him, Allah is more generous than to return to something He has pardoned."
"776","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Habbah al-Urani, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, laugh upon the pulpit; I never saw him laugh a laugh greater than it, until his molars appeared. Then he said: I remembered the word of Abu Talib: Abu Talib appeared to us while I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we were praying in the belly of Nakhlah. He said: What are you doing, O son of my brother? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him to Islam, and he said: There is no harm in what you do or what you say, but by Allah my backside will never rise above me. And he laughed in wonder at the word of his father. Then he said: O Allah, I do not acknowledge that a servant of Yours of this community worshipped You before me other than Your Prophet, three times; I prayed before people prayed seven years."
"777","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father, and most of my knowledge, Allah willing, is that I heard it from him: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once led us in prayer then left; then he came with his head dripping water and led us in prayer, then said: I led you just now while junub; whoever is afflicted with what afflicted me or finds a stirring in his belly, let him do as I did."
"778","Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: My father used to converse at night with Ali; and Ali used to wear summer clothes in winter and winter clothes in summer. It was said to him: Why not ask him? So he asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me while my eyes were sore on the day of Khaybar. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyes are sore. He said: So he spat in my eyes and said: O Allah, remove from him heat and cold. I have felt neither heat nor cold since that day. And he said: I shall surely give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love, who does not flee. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) craned for it, and he gave it to me."
"779","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Ishaq said: From Hani' ibn Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ammar came and sought permission. He said: Admit him; welcome to the good, the purified."
"780","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and others, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani', he said: I asked A'ishah about wiping over the leather socks, and she said: Ask Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. So I asked him, and he said: Three days and their nights, meaning for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"781","Ibn al-Ashja'i narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani', he said: Ali commanded me to wipe over the leather socks."
"782","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was saying upon the pulpit: By Allah, we have no book to recite to you except the Book of Allah the Exalted and this sheet hanging from his sword; I took it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); in it are the ordinances of charity, hanging from a sword of his whose ornament is iron, or he said: Whose pulleys are iron, meaning its rings."
"783","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal al-Hashimi said: My father al-Harith was in charge of an affair of Mecca in the time of Uthman. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, came to Mecca. Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: So I met Uthman at al-Nuzul at Qudayd; the people of the water hunted partridges and cooked them with water and salt and made them broth for tharid, and we presented them to Uthman and his companions, and they held back. Uthman said: Game I did not hunt nor ordered to be hunted; people in ihram-free state hunted it and fed it to us, so what harm? Uthman said: Who speaks on this? They said: Ali. He sent for Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he came. Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: As if I am looking at Ali when he came while brushing dry fodder from his hands. Uthman said to him: Game we did not hunt nor ordered to be hunted; people in ihram-free state hunted it and fed it to us, so what harm? He said: So Ali became angry and said: I adjure by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was brought a leg of wild donkey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are a people in ihram, so feed it to the people in ihram-free state. He said: So twelve men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified. Then Ali said: I adjure by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was brought ostrich eggs, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are a people in ihram; feed it to the people in ihram-free state. He said: So less than the number of the twelve testified. He said: So Uthman drew his leg back from the food, entered his tent, and the people of the water ate that food."
"784","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that his father was in charge of the food of Uthman. He said: As if I am looking at the partridges around the bowls. A man came and said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, dislikes this. He sent for Ali while he was smearing his hands with dry fodder. He said: You contradict us much. Ali said: I remind by Allah one who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought the rump of a wild donkey while in ihram, and he said: We are in ihram, so feed it to the people in ihram-free state. Men stood and testified. Then he said: I remind by Allah a man who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought five eggs of ostrich, and he said: We are in ihram, so feed it to the people in ihram-free state. Men stood and testified. Uthman stood, entered his tent, and they left the food to the people of the water."
"785","Hashim narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that he said: A mule was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a gift. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if we mated donkeys with our horses they would bring us the like of this. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only those who do not know do that."
"786","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Witr is not obligatory, but a practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Odd and loves the odd."
"787","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from his master Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I performed Umrah with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, in the time of Umar or the time of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him. He stayed with his sister Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib. When he finished his Umrah he returned, and washing water was poured for him and he washed. When he finished his washing, a group of the people of Iraq entered upon him and said: O Abu Hasan, we came to ask you about a matter we wish you to inform us of. He said: I think al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah tells you that he was the last of people in covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Yes, about that we came to ask you. He said: The last of people in covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Qutham ibn al-Abbas."
"788","Affan narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Utaybah narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Asram, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man of the people of Suffah died and left two dinars or two dirhams. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands; pray over your companion."
"789","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever lies deliberately about a dream will be burdened with tying a grain of barley on the Day of Resurrection."
"790","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Umarah ibn Ruwaybah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People follow Quraysh; their righteous follow their righteous, and their wicked follow their wicked."
"791","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, a man of Banu Sadus called Jurayy ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the slit ear and horn of the sacrificial animal. He said: So I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: Half, and what is above that."
"792","Affan narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu al-Miqdam, from Abd al-Rahman al-Azraq, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was sleeping on the bed. Al-Hasan or al-Husayn asked for drink. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to a young sheep of ours and milked it, and it yielded milk. Al-Hasan came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved him aside. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, as if he is the more beloved of them to you. He said: No, but he asked for drink before him. Then he said: I and you and these two and this sleeper shall be in one place on the Day of Resurrection."
"793","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to me, Hudayj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hudhayfah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I went out when the moon rose as if a half bowl, and said: Tonight is the Night of Decree."
"794","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Zad han, that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a spot of a hair of his body of major impurity untouched by water, such and such of the Fire will be done to him. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: From then I became hostile to my head."
"795","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zad han, that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, drank standing, and people looked at him as if they disapproved. He said: What are you looking at? If I drink standing, I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing; and if I drink sitting, I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink sitting."
"796","Affan and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large of head, great of eyes, long of eyelashes, Hasan said: Eyelids, his eyes tinged with redness, thick of beard, bright of complexion, thick of hands and feet; when he walked as if walking uphill, Hasan said: Leaning forward; and when he turned he turned all together."
"797","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, and he said to me: It is my name and kunyah: Malik ibn Su'ayr, meaning Ibn al-Khims, narrated to us, Furat ibn Ahnaf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, stood as a speaker in al-Rahbah, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said what Allah willed him to say, then called for a cup of water, rinsed his mouth from it, wiped, and drank the remainder of his cup while standing, then said: It reached me that a man of you dislikes drinking while standing; and this is the ablution of one who has not broken it; and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do thus."
"798","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: We have nothing of revelation, or he said: A book from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except what is in the Book of Allah and this sheet joined to my sword; and upon him was a sword whose ornament is iron; and in it are the ordinances of charities."
"799","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, that Ali was told: The killer of al-Zubayr is at the door. He said: Let the killer of the son of Safiyyah enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple."
"800","Affan and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me two brother slaves as a gift; I sold one of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did the two slaves do? I said: I sold one of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return him."
"801","Affan and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, Affan said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in seven garments."
"802","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Fudalah ibn Abi Fudalah al-Ansari, and Abu Fudalah was among the people of Badr, he said: I went out with my father visiting Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, for an illness that had befallen him and weighed heavily upon him, he said: So my father said to him: What keeps you in this house of yours, if your appointed time were to come to you none would take charge of you except Bedouins of Juhaynah, you would be carried to Madinah, but if your appointed time comes to you your companions will take charge of you and pray over you. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me that I shall not die until I am placed in command, then this, meaning his beard, will be dyed from the blood of this, meaning his head. Then he was killed, and Abu Fudalah was killed with Ali on the day of Siffin."
"803","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abdulaziz, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us from his uncle al-Majishun ibn Abi Salamah from al-Araj from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he opened the prayer would say the takbir then say: I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, inclining to truth, and I am not among the polytheists. Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, He has no partner, and with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You, You are my Lord and I am Your servant, I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins, none forgives sins but You. O Allah, guide me to the best of character, none guides to the best of it but You, and turn away from me the evil of it, none turns away from me the evil of it but You. Here I am at Your service and all good is in Your hands, and evil is not to You, I am by You and to You, blessed are You and exalted, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. And when he bowed he said: O Allah, to You I have bowed and in You I have believed and to You I have submitted, my hearing and my sight and my brain and my bones and my sinews have humbled themselves to You. And when he raised his head he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, and to You belongs praise filling the heavens and the earth and what is between them and filling whatever You will of anything after. And when he prostrated he said: O Allah, to You I have prostrated and in You I have believed and to You I have submitted, my face has prostrated to the One who created it and fashioned it and made its form excellent and split its hearing and sight, so blessed is Allah, the best of creators. And when he finished the prayer and gave salutation he said: O Allah, forgive me what I have done before and what I have done after and what I have concealed and what I have declared and what I have exceeded and what You know better of than I, You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, there is no god but You. Abdullah said: It has reached us from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl that he said concerning this hadith, and evil is not to You, he said: Evil is not a means of nearness to You."
"804","Hujayn narrated to us: Abdulaziz narrated to us from his uncle al-Majishun ibn Abi Salamah from Abdurrahman al-Araj from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he opened the prayer he said the takbir then said: I have turned my face, then he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: and turn away from me the evil of it."
"805","Hujayn narrated to us: Abdulaziz narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl al-Hashimi from al-Araj from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"806","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle: Abu Ubayd, the freedman of Abdurrahman ibn Azhar, informed me that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man that anything of the meat of his sacrifice should remain in his house after three days."
"807","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Suddi Ismail mentioning it from Abu Abdurrahman al-Sulami from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old uncle has died, he said: Go and bury him, then do not do anything until you come to me, he said: So I buried him then came to him, he said: Go and take a bath, then do not do anything until you come to me, he said: So I bathed then came to him, he said: So he supplicated for me with supplications that I would not like to have red and black camels in exchange for them, he said: And Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he washed the dead would take a bath."
"808","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warakani narrated to us in the year two hundred and twenty-seven: Abu Aqil Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Ha, and Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us in the year two hundred and forty: Abu Aqil Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us from Kathir al-Nawwa from Ibrahim ibn Hasan ibn Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father from his grandfather, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will appear in the end of time a people called al-Rafidah, they reject Islam."
"809","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to me: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seek permission, so if he was in prayer he would glorify Allah, and if he was not in prayer he would give me permission."
"810","Abdullah narrated to us: Abdul-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to me: Dawud ibn Abdurrahman al-Attar narrated to us: Abu Abdullah Maslamah al-Razi narrated to us from Abu Amr al-Bajali from Abdulmalik ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah loves the oft-tried oft-repentant servant."
"811","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warakani narrated to me: Abu Shihab al-Hannat, Abd Rabbih ibn Nafi, informed us from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Abu Yala from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the matter of madhiy perplexed me I ordered al-Miqdad to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, so he said: Wudu is due for it, out of shyness on account of Fatimah."
"812","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali from Ali that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar forbade mutah marriage and the flesh of donkeys."
"813","Yunus narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us from Asim from Zirr that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was told: The killer of al-Zubayr is at the door, so Ali said: The killer of the son of Safiyyah will surely enter the Fire, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam."
"814","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, stopped at Qudayd, and partridges in bowls raised upon their legs were brought to him, so he sent to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was tarring a camel of his, so he came with wood chips falling from his hands, so Ali refrained and the people refrained, so Ali said: Who here is from Ashja, do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought by a Bedouin ostrich eggs and a young wild ass, so he said: Feed them to your family, for we are in ihram, they said: Yes, so Uthman stepped back from his couch and came down and said: You have spoiled it for us."
"815","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Ali ibn Mudrik informed me, he said: I heard Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Abdullah ibn Nujayy from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog nor an image."
"816","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq informed us: I heard Hubayrah, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me, the gold ring and qassi silk and mitharah silk saddle cover."
"817","Affan narrated to us: Khalid, meaning al-Tahhan, narrated to us: Mutarrif narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man raise his voice with the Quran before the night prayer and after it, confusing his companions in prayer."
"818","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ali ibn Abi Talib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Blood money for the mukatab is paid in proportion to what he has paid toward his freedom."
"819","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he married him to Fatimah sent with her a blanket and a pillow of leather stuffed with fiber and two millstones and a waterskin and two jars."
"820","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us: al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Hasan ibn Sad from his father that Yuhannas and Safiyyah were among the captives of the fifth, then Safiyyah committed adultery with a man of the fifth and bore a boy, so the adulterer and Yuhannas claimed him, so they disputed to Uthman, so he referred them to Ali ibn Abi Talib, so Ali said: I judge concerning them with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone, and he lashed them both fifty fifty."
"821","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi from his mother, she said: We were at Mina when a crier cried: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Do not fast, for they are days of eating and drinking, she said: So I raised the ropes of the tent, and the crier was Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"822","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us from Hajjaj ibn Dinar from al-Hakam from Hujayyah ibn Adi from Ali that al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hastening his charity before it became due, so he permitted him that."
"823","Abdullah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me from his father from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: I sent al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he asked him about madhiy that comes out of a man, what should he do about it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform wudu and sprinkle water on your private part."
"824","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us from Ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi from his mother that she said: While we were at Mina, Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, was upon a camel saying: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Indeed these are days of eating and drinking, so let no one fast, so the people followed him."
"825","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed me more than once, he said: I heard Asim ibn Damrah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: From every part of the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr, from its beginning and its middle and its end, and his witr ended at the end of the night."
"826","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me, he said: I heard Hujayyah ibn Adi, a man from Kindah, he said: I heard a man ask Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I have bought this cow for sacrifice, for seven, he said: The horn, he said: It does not harm you, he said: Lameness, he said: When it reaches the place of slaughter then slaughter it, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear."
"827","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us: Sad ibn Ubaydah narrated to me, he said: Abu Abdurrahman al-Sulami and Hibban ibn Atiyyah disputed, so Abu Abdurrahman said to Hibban: You know what it was that emboldened your companion, meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: So what is it, may you have no father, he said: A statement I heard from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and al-Zubayr and Abu Marthad, and all of us were horsemen, he said: Go forth until you reach Rawdat Khakh, for in it is a woman with a letter from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to the polytheists, so bring her to me, so we went forth upon our horses until we reached her where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had told us, traveling upon a camel of hers, he said: And he had written to the people of Makkah of the march of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we said to her: Where is the letter that is with you, she said: I have no letter with me, so we made her camel kneel and searched in her baggage and found nothing in it, so my two companions said: We do not see any letter with her, so I said: You both know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not lie, then I swore: By the One by whom I swear, if you do not bring out the letter I shall surely strip you, so she reached for her waistband while she was girded with a cloak, and brought out the letter, so they brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, he has betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers, let me strike his neck, he said: O Hatib, what carried you to do what you did, he said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah there is nothing in me of not believing in Allah and His Messenger, but I wanted to have with the people a favor by which Allah would protect my family and my wealth, and there was none among your companions except he had there among his people one by whom Allah would protect his family and his wealth, he said: He has told the truth, so do not say to him but good, so Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, he has betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers, let me strike his neck, he said: Is he not among the people of Badr, and what informs you, perhaps Allah looked upon them and said: Do whatever you wish, for Paradise has become due for you, so the eyes of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, filled with tears, and he said: Allah and His Messenger know best."
"828","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, and I heard it myself from Harun: Ibn Wahb informed us: Said ibn Abdullah al-Juhani narrated to me that Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to him from his father from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, O Ali, do not delay them: prayer when its time comes, and the funeral when it is present, and the unmarried woman when she finds an equal match."
"829","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Mubaraki Sulayman ibn Muhammad, neighbor of Khalaf al-Bazzar, narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Abdulkarim from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Ibn Abbas from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the gold ring and wearing red and reciting in bowing and prostration."
"830","Abdullah narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from his father from Abdulkarim from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn Abbas from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought game meat while he was in ihram, so he did not eat it."
"831","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to me: Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Abdulkarim from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn Abbas from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me qassi garments and saddle covers and saffron-dyed cloth and reciting the Quran while a man is bowing or prostrating."
"832","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Muhammad Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to me, he came to us from Kufah: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us from al-Amash from Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, Ha, Abdullah said: And Said ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to me: My father narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: We disputed about a surah of the Quran, so we said thirty-five verses, thirty-six verses, he said: So we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, conversing with him, so we said: We have differed in recitation, so the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reddened, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders you to recite as you were taught."
"833","Abdullah narrated to us: Salih ibn Abdullah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Asim, Ha, and Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, al-Qawariri said in his hadith: Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us from Zirr, meaning Ibn Hubaysh, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet: Abu Bakr, then he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after Abu Bakr: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"834","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Salih Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to me at Makkah: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us from al-Shabi from Wahb al-Suwai, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: Who is the best of this ummah after its Prophet, so I said: You, O Commander of the Faithful, he said: No, the best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and we do not deem it far that tranquility speaks upon the tongue of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"835","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Mansur ibn Abdurrahman, meaning al-Ghudani al-Ashall, informed us from al-Shabi: Abu Juhayfah, whom Ali used to call Wahb al-Khayr, narrated to me, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Abu Juhayfah, shall I not inform you of the most excellent of this ummah after its Prophet, he said: I said: Yes, and I did not think that anyone was more excellent than him, he said: The most excellent of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, and after Abu Bakr is Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and after them is another third, and he did not name him."
"836","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Juhayfah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, and after Abu Bakr is Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and if I wished I would inform you of the third, I would do so."
"837","Abdullah narrated to us: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us: Khalid al-Zayyat narrated to us: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, he said: My father was among the police of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and was under the pulpit, so my father narrated to me that he ascended the pulpit, meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so he praised Allah and extolled Him and invoked blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, and the second is Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Allah places good where He loves."
"838","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he married him to Fatimah sent with him a blanket and a pillow of leather stuffed with fiber and two millstones and a waterskin and two jars, so Ali said to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them both, one day: By Allah I have drawn water until my chest has ached, he said: And Allah has brought your father captives, so go and seek a servant from him, so she said: And I, by Allah, have ground until my hands have blistered, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What has brought you, my daughter, she said: I have come to greet you, and she was shy to ask him, and returned, so he said: What did you do, she said: I was shy to ask him, so we came to him together, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I have drawn water until my chest has ached, and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I have ground until my hands have blistered, and Allah has brought you captives and plenty, so give us a servant, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah I shall not give you two and leave the people of the Suffah with their stomachs empty, I find nothing to spend on them, but I shall sell them and spend their prices on them, so they returned, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them while they had entered into their blanket, when it covered their heads their feet became uncovered, and when they covered their feet their heads became uncovered, so they rose, so he said: Stay in your place, then he said: Shall I not inform you two of better than what you asked me, they said: Yes, so he said: Words Jibril, peace be upon him, taught me, so he said: You two glorify Allah ten times and praise Allah ten times and magnify Allah ten times after every prayer, and when you go to your bed then glorify Allah thirty-three times and praise Allah thirty-three times and magnify Allah thirty-four times, he said: So by Allah I have not left them since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them to me, he said: So Ibn al-Kawwa said to him: Not even the night of Siffin, so he said: May Allah fight you, O people of Iraq, yes, not even the night of Siffin."
"839","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Shabi that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged Shurahah on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and said: I flog her by the Book of Allah and stone her by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"840","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, I and two men, a man from my people and a man from Banu Asad I think, so he sent them both forth and said: Indeed you two are stout, so strive for your religion, then he entered the privy and relieved himself, then came out and took a handful of water and wiped himself with it, then began reciting the Quran, he said: So it was as if he saw that we disapproved of that, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself then come out and recite the Quran and eat meat with us, and nothing barred him from the Quran except janabah."
"841","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abdullah ibn Salamah from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was saying: O Allah, if my appointed time has come then relieve me, and if it is delayed then raise me, and if it is a trial then make me patient, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you say, so he repeated to him what he had said, he said: So he struck him with his foot and said: O Allah, grant him health, or: O Allah, heal him, Shubah doubted, he said: So I did not complain of that pain of mine after."
"842","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us from Shubah from Abu Ishaq: I heard Asim ibn Damrah narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Witr is not obligatory like the prayer, but it is a sunnah, so do not leave it, Shubah said: And I found it written with me: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr."
"843","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik informed us from Abi al-Hasna from al-Hakam from Hanash from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sacrifice on his behalf, so I sacrifice on his behalf ever."
"844","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Jabir from al-Shabi from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury and its giver and its two witnesses and its writer and the tattooer and the tattooed for beautification and the withholder of charity and the muhallil and the one for whom muhallil marriage is done, and he used to forbid wailing."
"845","Abdurrazzaq informed us: Sufyan from Jabir from Abdullah ibn Nujayy from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I used to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every morning, so if he cleared his throat I entered, and if he was silent I did not enter, he said: So he came out to me and said: Last night something happened, I heard a rustling in the house, and there was Jibril, peace be upon him, so I said: What prevented you from entering the house, so he said: In the house is a dog, he said: So I entered and there was a puppy of al-Hasan under a chair of ours, he said: So he said: Indeed the angels do not enter the house if in it are three: a dog or an image or one in janabah."
"846","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith al-Awar from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to appoint anyone of my ummah without consultation I would appoint over them Ibn Umm Abd."
"847","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Rizam ibn Said al-Taymi narrated to us from Jawwab al-Taymi from Yazid ibn Sharik, meaning al-Taymi, from Ali, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: When you ejaculate then wash as for janabah, and if you are not ejaculating then do not wash."
"848","al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid al-Hamdani narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Abd al-Ala, narrated to us from Tariq ibn Ziyad, he said: We went out with Ali to the Khawarij, so he killed them, then he said: Look, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come out a people speaking the truth not passing their throats, they exit from the truth as the arrow exits from the target, their mark is that among them is a black man with a defective arm, on his arm are black hairs, if it is he then you have killed the worst of people, and if it is not he then you have killed the best of people, so we wept, then he said: Seek, so we sought and found the defective-armed man, so we fell prostrate and Ali fell prostrate with us, except that he said: Speaking the word of truth."
"849","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Abd al-Ala from Abu Abdurrahman from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And you make your provision, saying your gratitude is that you deny, saying: We were rained by such and such star and by such and such star."
"850","Muammal narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Abu Abdurrahman from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he raised it: And you make your provision, Muammal said: I said to Sufyan: Israil raised it, he said: Little boys, little boys."
"851","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Shurayh ibn al-Numan, Abu Ishaq said: And he was a truthful man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear and not to sacrifice a one-eyed animal nor a muqabalah nor a mudabarah nor a sharqa nor a kharqa, Zuhayr said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did he mention a broken-horned one, he said: No, I said: What is muqabalah, he said: The tip of the ear is cut, I said: What is mudabarah, he said: The rear of the ear is cut, I said: What is sharqa, he said: The ear is split, I said: What is kharqa, he said: Its ear is pierced by the brand."
"852","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to appoint anyone of my ummah without consultation from them I would appoint over them Ibn Umm Abd."
"853","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, and Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, both saying: Zaidah narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us from his father from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, in a blanket and a waterskin and a pillow of leather stuffed with fiber, Muawiyah said: Idhkhir grass, my father said: And khamilah is a velvety blanket."
"854","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil informed us from Abu Ishaq from Hani ibn Hani, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: al-Hasan most resembles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between the chest to the head, and al-Husayn most resembles below that."
"855","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us from Mansur ibn Hayyan from Abi al-Tufayl, he said: We said to Ali: Inform us of something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided to you, so he said: He did not confide to me anything he concealed from the people, but I heard him saying: Allah curses whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah curses whoever shelters an innovator, and Allah curses whoever curses his parents, and Allah curses whoever changes the boundaries of the earth, meaning the landmarks."
"856","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Hani ibn Hani from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so when I emitted madhiy I bathed, so I ordered al-Miqdad, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he laughed and said: Wudu is due for it."
"857","Aswad, meaning Ibn Amir, narrated to us: Israil informed us from Abu Ishaq from Hani ibn Hani from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Jafar and Zayd, he said: So he said to Zayd: You are my freedman, so he hopped, he said: And he said to Jafar: You resemble my creation and my character, he said: So he hopped behind Zayd, he said: And he said to me: You are from me and I am from you, he said: So I hopped behind Jafar."
"858","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sulayman narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us from Mansur ibn Hayyan, he said: I heard Amir ibn Wathilah, he said: It was said to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: Inform us of something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided to you, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not confide to me anything and conceal it from the people, but I heard him saying: Allah curses whoever reviles his parents, and Allah curses whoever changes the boundaries of the earth, and Allah curses whoever shelters an innovator."
"859","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Jafar, meaning al-Farra, narrated to me from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Yuthay from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who shall be appointed after you, he said: If you appoint Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, you will find him trustworthy, ascetic in the world, desirous of the Hereafter, and if you appoint Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, you will find him strong, trustworthy, not fearing in Allah the blame of a blamer, and if you appoint Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and I do not see you doing so, you will find him a guide, guided, taking you by the straight path."
"860","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi al-Tayyah, he said: I heard a man from Anazah narrating from a man from Banu Asad, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came out to us and said: Indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded witr, its witr is established this hour, O Ibn al-Nabbah, call the adhan or call the repetition."
"861","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi al-Tayyah: A man from Anazah narrated to me from a man from Banu Asad, he said: Ali came out when the caller called the repetition for the dawn prayer and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us witr, so it is established for him this hour, then he said: Establish the prayer, O Ibn al-Nawwahah."
"862","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi al-Tayyah: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl al-Anazi narrating from a man from Banu Asad, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came out to us, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Suwayd ibn Said: I was with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was covered in his garment."
"863","Hashim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: I heard Abu Burdah narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing a ring in this or this, the middle and the index, and Jabir, meaning al-Jufi, said: It is the middle, there is no doubt in it."
"864","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Jabir from Abdullah ibn Nujayy from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing an animal with broken horn and ear."
"865","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zakariyya narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Hani ibn Hani from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, used to lower his voice when he recited, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to raise his recitation, and Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he recited would take from this surah and this, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: Why do you lower your voice, he said: Indeed I make heard the One to whom I confide, and he said to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Why do you raise your recitation, he said: I frighten Satan and awaken the drowsy, and he said to Ammar: And why do you take from this surah and this, he said: Do you hear me mixing with it what is not from it, he said: No, he said: Then all of it is good."
"866","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warakani narrated to me: Abu Mashar Najih al-Madani, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was placed between the pulpit and the grave, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came until he stood before the rows and said: He is this, three times, then he said: May the mercy of Allah be upon you, there is none of the creation of Allah more beloved to me to meet with his record after the record of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this one covered in his garment."
"867","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Said al-Harawi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abi Yafur narrated to us from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah from his father, he said: I was with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was covered with his garment, having died, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came and uncovered the garment from his face then said: May the mercy of Allah be upon you, Abu Hafs, for by Allah none remains after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more beloved to me to meet Allah with his record than you."
"868","Ubaydah ibn Humayd al-Taymi Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us: Rukayn narrated to me from Husayn ibn Qabisah from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I used to bathe in winter until my back cracked, he said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or it was mentioned to him, he said: So he said: Do not do so, when you see madhiy then wash your organ and perform your wudu for prayer, so when you spurt water then bathe."
"869","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he was asked about that, so he said: For madhiy is wudu, and for maniy is bathing."
"870","Ubaydah narrated to us: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to me from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I ordered a man, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, so he said: Wudu is due for it."
"871","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to me: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Asim from Zirr from Abu Juhayfah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, then he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet and after Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: Umar."
"872","Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us: Amir ibn al-Simt narrated to me from Abi al-Gharif, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought water for wudu, so he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times and washed his face three times and washed his hands and forearms three times three times, then wiped his head, then washed his feet, then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu, then he recited something of the Quran then said: This is for one who is not in janabah, as for one in janabah then not, not even a verse."
"873","Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us: Rabiah ibn Utbah al-Kinani narrated to us from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, wiped his head in wudu until it was about to drip, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu."
"874","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Imran al-Wasiti narrated to me: Sharik narrated to us from Mikhariq from Tariq, meaning Ibn Shihab, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: We have no book we recite to you except what is in the Quran and what is in this paper, a paper that was in the sheath of a sword on which was an iron ornament, I took it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in it are the ordinances of charity."
"875","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi Luwayn narrated to me: Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: Abdurrahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Zayd al-Suwai from Abu Juhayfah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Indeed part of the Sunnah in prayer is placing the palms upon the palms under the navel."
"876","Marwan narrated to us: Abdulmalik ibn Sila al-Hamdani narrated to us from Abd Khayr, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, taught us the wudu of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the boy poured upon his hands until he cleaned them, then he put his hand into the water skin and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and washed his face three times three times and his forearms to the elbows three times three times, then he put his hand into the water skin and immersed its lower part with his hand then took it out and wiped the other with it, then wiped his head once with his palms, then washed his feet to the ankles three times three times, then he scooped a little water with his palm and drank it, then he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform wudu."
"877","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zakariyya narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Asim ibn Damrah from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people of the Quran, pray witr, for Allah is Witr and loves witr."
"878","Abdullah narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us from Bayan from Amir from Abu Juhayfah, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, then Umar, then another man."
"879","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abd Khayr from Ali, and from al-Shabi from Abu Juhayfah from Ali, and from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah from his father from Ali that he said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and the best of it after Abu Bakr is Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and if I wished I would name the third."
"880","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ibn Abi Khalid, Ha, and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us from al-Shabi from Abu Juhayfah: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and if I wished I would tell you of the third."
"881","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me from Abu Muhammad from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Madinah and ordered him to level the graves."
"882","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Simak from Hanash from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, he said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me to a people older than me while I am young, I do not discern judgment, he said: So he placed his hand upon my chest and said: O Allah, make his tongue firm and guide his heart, O Ali, when two litigants sit to you then do not judge between them until you hear from the other as you heard from the first, for if you do that the judgment will become clear to you, he said: So no judgment differed for me after, or no judgment was obscure to me after."
"883","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Minhal from Abbad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When this verse came down: And warn your nearest kin, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered of his household, so thirty gathered, and they ate and drank, he said: So he said to them: Who guarantees my debt and my promises on my behalf and will be with me in Paradise and will be my successor among my family, so a man, Sharik did not name him, said: O Messenger of Allah, you were a sea, who can undertake this, he said: Then the other said it, he said: So he presented that to his household, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I."
"884","Aswad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Harith from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr at the adhan and pray the two rakahs at the iqamah."
"885","Aswad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Asim from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray by day sixteen rakahs."
"886","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi from Ali ibn Abi Talib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ride a donkey named Ufayr."
"887","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid al-Himsi narrated to us: al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to me from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah from Abdurrahman ibn Aidh al-Azdi from Ali ibn Abi Talib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed the posterior is the tie of the eye, so whoever sleeps let him perform wudu."
"888","Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us: Ibn Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan al-Janbi narrated to me from his father from his grandfather from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When I killed Marhab I came with his head to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"889","Abdullah narrated to us: Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Yunus ibn Khabbab informed us from Jarir ibn Hayyan from his father that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to his father: I shall surely send you with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with: to level every grave and to efface every idol."
"890","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Wudu is due for it."
"891","Abdullah narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me: Khalid informed us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: For it is wudu, and for maniy is bathing."
"892","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Ibn al-Asbahani from a grandmother of his, and she was a concubine of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, she said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was a sleepy man, and when I prayed Maghrib in my clothes I slept, then Yahya ibn Said said: So I sleep before Isha, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he permitted me."
"893","Abdullah narrated to us: Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to us: Abdulaziz ibn Muslim, meaning Abu Zayd al-Qasmali, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he said: For madhiy is wudu, and for maniy is bathing."
"894","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Bahili Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas narrated to me: Abdulwahhab, meaning al-Thaqafi, narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Abdulkarim and Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with him his sacrificial animals, so he ordered him to give in charity their meat and their skins and their coverings."
"895","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Hawshab mentioned from Abu Ishaq from Abd Khayr from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led, and Abu Bakr prayed next, and Umar made three, may Allah be pleased with him, then a trial struck us, may Allah pardon whom He wills."
"896","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan narrated to us: Shurayh, meaning Ibn Ubayd, narrated to me, he said: The people of Sham were mentioned before Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was in Iraq, so they said: Curse them, O Commander of the Faithful, he said: No, indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Abdal will be in Sham, and they are forty men, whenever a man dies Allah replaces in his place a man, by them rain is given and by them victory is granted over the enemies and punishment is turned away from the people of Sham by them."
"897","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Said al-Harawi narrated to me: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Mujahid from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with the sacrificial camels, he said: Do not give the butcher anything from them."
"898","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn informed us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was placed upon his bier, so the people gathered around him supplicating and praying before he was lifted, and I was among them, so nothing startled me but a man who took my shoulder from behind me, so I turned and it was Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, so he asked mercy for Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: You have left none more beloved to me to meet Allah with the like of his deed than you, by Allah indeed I thought Allah will surely join you with your two companions, and that is because I often heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I went, I and Abu Bakr and Umar, and I entered, I and Abu Bakr and Umar, and I came out, I and Abu Bakr and Umar, and indeed I thought Allah will surely join you with them."
"899","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah informed us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that he used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So when I found him praying he glorified Allah so I entered, and when he was not praying he gave permission."
"900","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb informed us from al-Zuhri: Ali ibn Husayn informed me that Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knocked on him and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at night and said: Will you not pray, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, our souls are but in the hand of Allah, so when He wills to raise us He raises us, so he turned away when I said that and did not return anything to me, then I heard him while turning away striking his thigh saying: And man is most argumentative of all things."
"901","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Ali ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that his father Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him by night, he and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, then he mentioned the like of it."
"902","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us, my father said: I heard him narrating from Abdullah ibn Wahb, from his father, from Abu Khalifah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah is Gentle, loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"903","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever narrates from me a hadith that is seen to be a lie, he is one of the liars."
"904","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abidah, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a small hand, or a deformed hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I said to Ali: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"905","Mansur ibn Wardan al-Asadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When this verse was revealed: And pilgrimage to the House is a duty upon mankind toward Allah for whoever can find a way to it, they said: O Messenger of Allah, is it every year? He was silent. They said: Is it every year? He was silent. He said: Then they said: Is it every year? He said: No, and if I said yes it would become obligatory. Then Allah the Exalted revealed: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made manifest to you, would distress you, to the end of the verse."
"906","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani, he said: I asked Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about wiping, and she said: Go to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, for he is more knowledgeable about that than I. He said: So I came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about wiping over the khuffs. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command us to wipe over the khuffs for a day and a night, and for the traveler three."
"907","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, he raised it."
"908","Abdullah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali al-Azdi narrated to me, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Shubah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Khayr: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"909","Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Said, the brother of Sufyan, narrated to us, from his father, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Khayr al-Hamdani, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying upon the minbar: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet? He said: Then he mentioned Abu Bakr. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the second? He said: Then he mentioned Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Then he said: If I wished I would inform you of the third. He said: And he fell silent, and we thought he meant himself. So I said: Did you hear him saying this? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, otherwise may these two become deaf."
"910","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Sala narrated to us, my father Abd al-Malik ibn Sala narrated to us, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, and said: This is the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"911","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of al-Ahzab: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer. May Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire. He said: Then he prayed it between the two Ishas, between Maghrib and Isha. And Abu Muawiyah once said, meaning between Maghrib and Isha."
"912","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a hadith, then to fall from the sky is dearer to me than to lie upon him. And when I narrate to you from others, I am but a man engaged in war, and war is deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will emerge at the end of time a people young in age, foolish in minds, speaking from the speech of the best of creation. Their faith will not pass their throats. Wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for whoever kills them on the Day of Resurrection."
"913","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I have exempted you from zakah on horses and slaves, and there is no zakah in less than two hundred."
"914","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abdurrahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you being selective among Quraysh and leaving us? He said: Do you have anything? I said: The daughter of Hamzah. He said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."
"915","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Ikrimah, he said: I moved from Muzdalifah with Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and I kept hearing him saying the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. So I asked him, and he said: I moved from Muzdalifah with my father, and I kept hearing him saying the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. So I asked him, and he said: I moved from Muzdalifah with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I kept hearing him saying the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"916","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Maysarah, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, drinking while standing. He said: So I said to him: You drink while standing? He said: If I drink standing, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drinking standing, and if I drink sitting, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drinking sitting."
"917","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I used to think that the soles of the feet were more deserving of wiping than their tops, until I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping their tops."
"918","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu as-Sawda, from Ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform wudu, and he washed the tops of his feet, and said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, washing the tops of his feet, I would have thought that their soles were more deserving of washing."
"919","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Uqbah Abu Kibran narrated to us, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: This is the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He performed wudu three times three times."
"920","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Umm Musa, she said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Ibn Masud to climb a tree, ordering him to bring him something from it. His companions looked at the leg of Abdullah ibn Masud when he climbed the tree and laughed at the thinness of his legs. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What are you laughing at? The leg of Abdullah is heavier in the scale on the Day of Resurrection than Uhud."
"921","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from a man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said on the day of al-Jamal: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not make a covenant to us regarding leadership that we would hold to, but it is something we considered on our own. Then Abu Bakr was appointed as successor, mercy of Allah upon Abu Bakr, and he stood firm and remained upright. Then Umar was appointed as successor, mercy of Allah upon Umar, and he stood firm and remained upright until religion became firmly established."
"922","Abdullah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me, Khalid informed us, from Ata, meaning Ibn as-Saib, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet? Abu Bakr, and the best after Abu Bakr is Umar, then Allah places good wherever He loves."
"923","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from one who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Ibn Masud saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged by preemption of the neighbor."
"924","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from wearing qassi garments, from reciting in bowing and prostration, and from wearing saffron-dyed garments."
"925","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Three men came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. One of them said: I had one hundred uqiyyah and I spent ten uqiyyahs from it. Another said: I had one hundred dinars and I gave ten dinars from it in charity. And the other said: I had ten dinars and I gave one dinar from it in charity. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are equal in reward; each one of you gave a tenth of his wealth in charity."
"926","Abdullah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Husayn, from al-Musayyab ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, he said: Ali stood and said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr and Umar, and we have introduced innovations after them; Allah the Exalted will decree concerning them what He wills."
"927","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar and ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: Witr is not obligatory like the prescribed prayer, but it is a sunnah which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, practiced."
"928","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Qasim al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wudu three times three times."
"929","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr at the time of the adhan."
"930","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabiah, he said it once. Abdurrazzaq said: And most of the time he says: One who witnessed Ali informed me when he rode. When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said: In the name of Allah. When he sat upright, he said: Praise be to Allah. Then he said: Glory be to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return. Then he praised Allah three times and said takbir three times. Then he said: O Allah, there is no god but You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. Then he laughed. He said: So it was said: What makes you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do the like of what I did and say the like of what I said, then he laughed. So we said: What makes you laugh, O Prophet of Allah? He said: The servant, or he said: I am amazed at the servant, when he says: There is no god but You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You; he knows that none forgives sins but He."
"931","Hajjaj narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani and Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, that the daughter of Hamzah followed them calling: O uncle, O uncle. So Ali took her, held her hand, and said to Fatimah: Take your cousin, attend to her. Then Ali, Zayd, and Jafar disputed concerning her. Ali said: I took her, and she is the daughter of my uncle. Jafar said: The daughter of my uncle, and her maternal aunt is under me. Zayd said: The daughter of my brother. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged her for her maternal aunt and said: The maternal aunt is like the mother. Then he said to Ali: You are from me and I am from you. And he said to Jafar: You resemble my appearance and my character. And he said to Zayd: You are our brother and our freed slave. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry the daughter of Hamzah? He said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."
"932","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"933","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shubah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet? Abu Bakr, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"934","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, as-Subayy ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet? Abu Bakr, and the second is Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. And if I wished I would name the third. Abu Ishaq said: Abd Khayr spelled it out so that you would not doubt what Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said."
"935","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu as-Sabah, from a man of Hamdan called Abu Aflah, from Ibn Zurayr, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took silk and placed it in his right hand, and took gold and placed it in his left, then said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah."
"936","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sulaym az-Zuraqi, from Asim ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until when we were at al-Harrah at as-Suqya which belonged to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring me water for wudu. When he performed wudu, he stood, faced the qiblah, then said takbir, then said: O Allah, Ibrahim was Your servant and Your friend; he supplicated for the people of Makkah for blessing. And I am Muhammad, Your servant and Your Messenger; I call upon You for the people of Madinah, to bless them in their mudd and their sa double what You blessed the people of Makkah with, along with blessing, two blessings."
"937","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Muzani informed us, a shaykh from Banu Tamim narrated to us, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us, or he said: Ali said: There will come upon people a biting time in which the wealthy will cling to what is in his hands. He said: And he was not commanded with that. Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: And do not forget generosity between you. And the wicked will rise, and the good will be humiliated, and the compelled will sell. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of the compelled, the sale of uncertainty, and the sale of fruit before it ripens."
"938","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Waki narrated to us. And Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of its women is Khadijah, and the best of its women is Maryam."
"939","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Mubaraki Sulayman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me from a gold ring, from wearing red, and from reciting in bowing and prostration."
"940","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he reaches puberty, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the afflicted until it is removed from him."
"941","Hushaym narrated to us, Ismail ibn Salim narrated to us, from ash-Shabi, he said: A married adulterer was brought to Ali, so he flogged him on Thursday one hundred lashes, then stoned him on Friday. So it was said to him: You combined two punishments upon him. He said: I flogged him by the Book of Allah and stoned him by the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"942","Hushaym and Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib narrated to us, from Hushaym, Husayn informed us, from ash-Shabi, he said: A freed slave woman of Said ibn Qays, married, who had committed adultery, was brought to Ali. He said: So he struck her one hundred, then stoned her, then said: I flogged her by the Book of Allah and stoned her by the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"943","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sharik, from as-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, call for water for wudu, wipe himself with it lightly, and wipe over the tops of his feet, then said: This is the wudu of one who did not break his ablution. Then he said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the tops of his feet, I would have thought that their soles were more deserving. Then he drank the remainder of his wudu water while standing, then said: Where are those who claim that no one should drink standing?"
"944","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Ismail the son of the daughter of as-Suddi narrated to me, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he described the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: He was great of head, white tinged with redness, with a great beard, large joints, coarse hands and feet, with a long line of hair on the chest, abundant head hair with wavy hair, walking with a forward lean as if descending a slope, neither tall nor short. I never saw the like of him, neither before him nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And Ali ibn Hakim said in his hadith: And Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, described to us the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: He was large of head, with good wavy hair."
"945","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Qasim al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wudu three times three times."
"946","Abdullah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih ibn Said, or Said, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was neither short nor tall, great of head with wavy hair, with a great beard tinged with redness, with a long line of hair on the chest, large joints, coarse hands and feet. When he walked he leaned forward as if descending a slope. I never saw the like of him before him nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"947","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu ash-Shaatha Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sulayman narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Uthman, from Abu Abdullah al-Makki, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about the description of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Neither short nor tall, his color tinged with redness, with good wavy hair, large joints, coarse hands, large of head, with a long line of hair on the chest. When he walked he leaned forward as if descending a slope. I never saw the like of him before him nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"948","Hajjaj narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When we arrived at Madinah, we ate from its fruits and found them unwholesome, and we were stricken with fever there. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek news about Badr. When it reached us that the idolaters had advanced, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, marched to Badr, and Badr is a well. The idolaters beat us to it. We found in it two men of them, a man of Quraysh and a freed slave of Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt. As for the Qurashi, he escaped, and as for the freed slave of Uqbah, we seized him. We began saying to him: How many are the people? He would say: By Allah, they are many in number, severe in might. When he said that, the Muslims beat him until they brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said to him: How many are the people? He said: By Allah, they are many in number, severe in might. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, endeavored to get him to tell how many they were, but he refused. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked him: How many camels do they slaughter? He said: Ten each day. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people are one thousand, each camel for one hundred, and he followed it. Then a light rain fell upon us at night, so we went under the trees and the leather shields to shelter under them from the rain. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spent the night supplicating his Lord the Mighty and Majestic, saying: O Allah, if You destroy this band, You will not be worshiped. He said: When dawn broke, he called: Prayer, O servants of Allah. So the people came from under the trees and the shields. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer and urged fighting. Then he said: The host of Quraysh is under this red hillside of the mountain. When the people drew near us and we lined up against them, there was a man among them on a red camel of his, riding among the people. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Ali, call Hamzah to me; he was the nearest of them to the idolaters: Who is the man of the red camel, and what is he saying to them? Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If there is among the people one who commands good, perhaps it is the man of the red camel. So Hamzah came and said: He is Utbah ibn Rabiah, and he is forbidding fighting and saying to them: O people, I see a people who have devoted themselves to death; you will not reach them while good remains among you. O people, tie it today to my head, and say: Utbah ibn Rabiah has become cowardly, though you know I am not the most cowardly of you. Abu Jahl heard that and said: You say this? By Allah, if another than you said this, I would bite him. Your lungs have filled your belly with fear. Utbah said: Is it me you revile, O one with a dyed backside? Today you will know which of us is the coward. He said: So Utbah, his brother Shaybah, and his son al-Walid came forward out of zeal and said: Who will duel? Six youths of the Ansar came out. Utbah said: We do not want these, but let men of our cousins of Banu Abd al-Muttalib duel us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Stand, O Ali, and stand, O Hamzah, and stand, O Ubaydah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib. So Allah the Exalted killed Utbah and Shaybah, the sons of Rabiah, and al-Walid ibn Utbah, and Ubaydah was wounded. So we killed seventy of them and captured seventy. A short man of the Ansar came with al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib as a captive. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, this one did not capture me; a bald man of the most handsome of people in face, upon a piebald horse, captured me, whom I do not see among the people. The Ansari said: I captured him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Be silent, for Allah the Exalted has supported you with a noble angel. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So we captured, and we captured of Banu Abd al-Muttalib: al-Abbas, Aqil, and Nawfal ibn al-Harith."
"949","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, he said: I asked Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and said: Inform me of a man among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whom I can ask about wiping over the khuffs. She said: Go to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and ask him, for he used to stay close to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to wipe over our khuffs when we travel."
"950","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb and from Zayd ibn Yuthay, they said: Ali called upon the people in ar-Rahbah: Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm, let him stand. He said: So six stood from the side of Said and six from the side of Zayd. They testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Is not Allah more entitled to the believers? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, whoever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."
"951","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr Dhu Murr, with the like of the hadith of Abu Ishaq, meaning from Said and Zayd, and he added in it: And support whoever supports him, and forsake whoever forsakes him."
"952","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali informed us, Sharik informed us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"953","Hajjaj narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When al-Hasan was born, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: I named him Harb. He said: Rather he is Hasan. When al-Husayn was born, he said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: I named him Harb. He said: Rather he is Husayn. When the third was born, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them by the names of the sons of Harun: Shabbar, Shabbayr, and Mushabbir."
"954","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah narrating from Abu at-Tufayl, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, single you out with anything? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not single us out with anything that he did not make general to all people, except what is in the sheath of this sword of mine. He said: So he brought out a sheet on which was written: May Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and may Allah curse whoever steals the landmarks of the land, and may Allah curse whoever curses his father, and may Allah curse whoever shelters an innovator."
"955","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata. Affan said: Yala ibn Ata informed us, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Amr ibn Hurayth, that he visited Hasan, and Ali was with him. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do you visit Hasan while there is in the heart what is in it? He said: Yes, you are not the lord of my heart to turn it wherever you wish. He said: That does not prevent me from giving you sincere counsel. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: No Muslim visits a Muslim except that Allah sends seventy thousand angels praying for him, at whatever hour of the day it is, until evening, and at whatever hour of the night it is, until morning."
"956","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan al-Basri, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the feeble-minded, or he said: the insane, until he regains reason, and from the child until he grows up."
"957","Bahz and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us. Bahz said: Hisham ibn Amr al-Fazari informed us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot count praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"958","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed me, I heard Mujahid narrating from Ibn Abi Layla: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: A silk suit was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he sent it to me. So I wore it, and I saw dislike on his face. So he commanded me, and I tore it into head coverings among the women."
"959","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abu Hassan, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would give a command, and it would be carried out, then it would be said: We have done such and such. He would say: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. He said: Al-Ashtar said to him: This that you say has spread among the people; is it something the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to you? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not entrust to me anything special apart from the people, except something I heard from him, and it is in a sheet in the sheath of my sword. He said: They kept pressing him until he brought out the sheet. He said: And in it was: Whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither repentance nor ransom will be accepted from him. He said: And in it was: Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred, and I declare Madinah sacred; what is between its two lava plains is sacred, and its preserve is all sacred. Its grass is not to be cut, its game is not to be frightened, its lost property is not to be picked up except for one who announces it, no tree of it is to be cut except that a man feed his camel with it, and no weapon is to be carried in it for fighting. He said: And in it was: The believers, their blood is equal, the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf, and they are one hand against others. No believer is to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant."
"960","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Abdurrahman al-Araj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he bowed, said: O Allah, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted. You are my Lord; my hearing, my sight, my brain, my bone, my sinew, and what my feet carry, have humbled themselves to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"961","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in ar-Rahbah calling upon the people: I adjure by Allah whoever heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master, let him stand and testify. Abdurrahman said: So twelve Badri men stood, as if I am looking at one of them. They said: We testify that we heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves, and my wives are their mothers? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So whoever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."
"962","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, upon the minbar delivering a sermon, wearing a sword whose ornament was iron. I heard him saying: By Allah, we have no book that we read to you except the Book of Allah the Exalted and this sheet which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me, containing the obligations of charity. He said, referring to a sheet attached to his sword."
"963","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Sumay informed us, from Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I was sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Sasah ibn Sawhan came, greeted, then stood and said: O Commander of the Faithful, forbid us what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade you. He said: He forbade us from dubba, hantam, muzaffat, and naqir, and he forbade us from qassi garments, red saddle cloths, silk, and gold rings. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, clothed me with a silk suit, so I went out in it for people to see upon me the clothing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me and commanded me to remove them both. So he sent one of them to Fatimah and divided the other among his women."
"964","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Nizar al-Ansi narrated to us, Simak ibn Ubayd ibn al-Walid al-Absi narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, and he narrated to me that he witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in ar-Rahbah. He said: I adjure by Allah a man who heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and witnessed him on the day of Ghadir Khumm, let him stand, and none stands except one who has seen him. So twelve men stood and said: We saw him and heard him when he took his hand, saying: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, oppose whoever opposes him, support whoever supports him, forsake whoever forsakes him. All stood except three who did not stand, so he supplicated against them, and his supplication befell them."
"965","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj ibn Minhal, narrated to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Ishaq, Abu Said narrated to me, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the caller to prayer calling, he said as he says. When he said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and that those who rejected Muhammad are the liars."
"966","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani, he said: I asked Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about wiping over the khuffs. She said: Ask Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I asked him, and he said: For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night. Yahya said: And he used to raise it, meaning Shubah, then he left it."
"967","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Ata, the freed slave of Umm Subayyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer, and I would delay the last Isha to the first third of the night. For when the first third of the night passes, Allah the Exalted descends to the lowest heaven and remains there until dawn rises. A caller says: Is there no asker to be given? Is there no supplicant to be answered? Is there no sick one seeking healing to be healed? Is there no sinner seeking forgiveness to be forgiven?"
"968","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, my uncle Abdurrahman ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"969","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: He was asked about witr, is it obligatory? He said: Not like the prescribed prayer, but it is a sunnah which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, practiced, and his companions, until they passed upon that."
"970","Ibn al-Ashjai narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sufyan, from as-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he called for a cup of water, then said: Where are those who claim they dislike drinking standing? He said: So he took it and drank while standing, then performed a light wudu and wiped over his sandals, then said: This is the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the pure who did not break his ablution."
"971","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he performed wudu three times three times and drank the remainder of his wudu water, then said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do."
"972","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isa, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And let those around him say: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs."
"973","Abdullah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr ad-Dabbi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam or Isa, Mansur doubted, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. And let whoever is with him say to him: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him reply to them: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs."
"974","Ghassan ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, Abu Israil narrated to us, from as-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came out to us while we were in the mosque and said: Where is the asker about witr? Whoever of us was in one rakah, he added another to it until we gathered to him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr at the beginning of the night, then performed witr in its middle, then established witr at this hour. He said: And that is at the appearance of dawn."
"975","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, he said: Abu Musa al-Ashari visited al-Hasan ibn Ali. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Did you come visiting the sick or visiting? Abu Musa said: Rather I came visiting the sick. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever visits a sick person in the morning, seventy thousand angels accompany him, all seeking forgiveness for him until evening, and he will have a harvest in Paradise. And if he visits him in the evening, seventy thousand angels accompany him, all seeking forgiveness for him until morning, and he will have a harvest in Paradise."
"976","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, he said: Abu Musa al-Ashari visited al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Did you come visiting the sick or visiting? He said: No, rather I came visiting the sick. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: There is no Muslim who visits a sick person except that seventy thousand angels go out with him, all seeking forgiveness for him, if he is in the morning until evening, and he will have a harvest in Paradise. And if he is in the evening, seventy thousand angels go out with him, all seeking forgiveness for him until morning, and he will have a harvest in Paradise."
"977","Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, meaning Abu Zayd al-Qasmaliy, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man who emitted much pre-seminal fluid, so I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that. He said: For pre-seminal fluid, wudu, and for semen, ghusl."
"978","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Mujalid, Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharahah had a husband absent in Sham, and she became pregnant. Her master brought her to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: She committed adultery. So she confessed. He flogged her on Thursday one hundred and stoned her on Friday, and dug for her up to the navel, and I was a witness. Then he said: Stoning is a sunnah which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, practiced. Had anyone testified against her, the witness would be the first to throw; he testifies then follows his testimony with his stone. But she confessed, so I am the first who stoned her. So he stoned her with a stone, then the people stoned, and I was among them. He said: By Allah, I was among those who killed her."
"979","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, from his father, from his uncle, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, and he was asked: May a man ride his sacrificial animal? He said: There is no harm in it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pass by men walking and command them to ride their sacrificial animals, and the sacrificial animal of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: And you do not follow anything better than the sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"980","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail, Amir narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of riba, its feeder, its two witnesses, its writer, the withholder of charity, the tattooing woman, the woman seeking tattooing, the one who marries to make lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful. He said: And he used to forbid wailing."
"981","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Purple saddle cloths, wearing qassi garments, and a gold ring were forbidden. Muhammad said: So I mentioned that to my brother Yahya ibn Sirin, and he said: Did you not hear this? Yes, and the edging of brocade."
"982","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, he said: Ali mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a small hand, or a deformed hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what Allah the Mighty and Majestic promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"983","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, he said: When Ali killed the people of Nahrawan, he said: Seek him. So they found him in a pit under the slain. They brought him out. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, turned to his companions and said: Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what Allah promised whoever kills these upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"984","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have exempted you from the charity on horses and slaves, and on silver is a quarter of a tenth."
"985","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When you are narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, think of him what is most guided, most suitable, and most God-fearing."
"986","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Misar, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abdurrahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When you are narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, think what is most suitable, most guided, and most God-fearing."
"987","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abdurrahman as-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When you are narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, think of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as most suitable, most God-fearing, and most guided. And Ali came out to us when the caller repeated the call, and said: Where is the asker about witr? This is a good time for witr."
"988","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abidah, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a small hand, or a deformed hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I said to Ali: Did you hear it? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"989","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Malik ibn Urfutah narrated to me, I heard Abd Khayr saying: I was with Ali, and a chair and a vessel were brought. He said: So he washed his hands three times, his face three times, his forearms three times, wiped his head, and Yahya described: He began with the front of his head to its back, and said: And I do not know whether he returned his hands or not. And he washed his feet. Then he said: Whoever loves to look at the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, this is the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Bakr al-Qatii said: Abu Abdurrahman said to us: Shubah erred in it; it is rather from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr."
"990","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq at-Tirmidhi narrated to me, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abidah as-Salmani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to think it was Fajr, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is the Asr prayer, meaning the middle prayer."
"991","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believers, their blood is equal, they are one hand against others, the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf. No believer is to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant."
"992","Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yusuf ibn Masud, from his grandmother, that a man passed by them upon a camel making it trot in Mina during the days of Tashriq: They are days of eating and drinking. So I asked about him, and they said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"993","Yahya narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Ubad, he said: I and al-Ashtar set out to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and we said: Did the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrust to you anything he did not entrust to the people generally? He said: No, except what is in this book of mine. He said: And a book in the sheath of his sword. And in it was: The believers, their blood is equal, they are one hand against others, the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf. No believer is to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant. Whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"994","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of al-Khandaq: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set, or the sun was about to set. May Allah fill their bellies, or their graves, with fire."
"995","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, my brother narrated to me, from my father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. And let it be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs. So I said to him: From my father? From Ayyub? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said."
"996","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to me, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, complained to me of blisters on her hands from grinding. So we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah complains to you of blisters on her hands from grinding and asks you for a servant. He said: Shall I not guide you both to what is better for you than a servant? So he commanded us at our sleep: thirty-three, thirty-three, and thirty-four of tasbih, tahmid, and takbir."
"997","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father, he said: I was informed from Sinan ibn Harun, Bayan narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bowed, if a cup of water were placed upon his back, it would not spill."
"998","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, performed wudu: he rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water three times from one hand, washed his face three times, then inserted his hand into the water skin, wiped his head, and washed his feet, then said: This is the wudu of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"999","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Ammar sought permission upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: The good, the purified."
"1000","Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Shubah. And Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Mansur. Yahya said: Mansur narrated to me, from Ribiy, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not lie upon me, for whoever lies upon me will enter the Fire. Hajjaj said: I said to Shubah: Did he meet Ali? He said: Yes, he narrated to me from Ali, and he did not say: He heard."
"1001","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, delivering a sermon, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"1002","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Hasan ibn Muslim and Abd al-Karim informed me that Mujahid informed them that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed him that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take charge of his sacrificial camels, and ordered him to distribute all of his camels, their meat, their skins, and their coverings, and not to give anything from them as payment for slaughtering."
"1003","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abd al-Karim, and he mentioned the hadith, and said: We give him the wage from ourselves."
"1004","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me a gold ring, reciting while bowing, al-qassi garments, and safflower-dyed garments."
"1005","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he prayed Zuhr, called for a cup of water in al-Rahbah, drank while standing, then said: Some men dislike this, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do, then he wiped with its remainder and said: This is the ablution of one who has not broken his ablution."
"1006","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is purification, its inviolability is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim."
"1007","Waki narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Uqbah Abu Kibran al-Muradi narrated to us, I heard Abd Khayr say: Ali said: Shall I not show you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he performed ablution three times three times."
"1008","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Sila narrated to us, my father Abd al-Malik ibn Sila narrated to us, he said: Abd Khayr used to lead us in Fajr, he said: One day we prayed Fajr behind Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and when he gave salam he stood, and we stood with him, and he walked until he reached al-Rahbah, sat, leaned his back against the wall, then raised his head and said: O Qanbar, bring me the water vessel and the basin, then he said to him: Pour, so he poured over him, and he washed his hands three times, put in his right hand, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times, then put in his hands and washed his face three times, then put in his right hand and washed his right forearm three times, then washed his left forearm three times, and said: This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1009","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: Ali said: I was a man who emitted much madhi, and I was shy to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the position of his daughter, so I ordered al-Miqdad and he asked him, and he said: He washes his private part and his testicles and performs ablution."
"1010","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mundhir Abu Yala, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered al-Miqdad and he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhi, and he said: He performs ablution."
"1011","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself, then eat meat with us and recite the Quran, and nothing would prevent him, or veil him, except janabah."
"1012","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray after every obligatory prayer two rakahs except Fajr and Asr, and Abd al-Rahman said: After every prayer."
"1013","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, who said: I used to think the inner feet were more deserving of wiping than the outer, until I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping the outer."
"1014","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Sawda, from Ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, who said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution, and he washed the tops of his feet, and said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wash the tops of his feet, I would have thought their bottoms were more deserving of washing."
"1015","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us another time, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution, and he wiped their tops."
"1016","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Uqbah Abu Kibran narrated to us, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, meaning: This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he performed ablution three times."
"1017","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransom anyone with his parents except Sad ibn Malik, for I heard him say to him on the day of Uhud: Shoot, O Sad, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"1018","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and put in command over them a man from the Ansar, and ordered them to listen to him and obey, he said: They angered him about something, so he said: Gather firewood for me, so they gathered firewood, then he said: Kindle a fire, so they kindled a fire for him, then he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not order you to listen to me and obey, they said: Yes, he said: Then enter it, he said: Some of them looked at others and said: We fled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the Fire, and they remained so until his anger subsided and the fire died, he said: When they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they mentioned that to him, and he said: Had they entered it they would never have come out of it, obedience is only in what is right."
"1019","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Kulayb, from Abu Burdah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to put the ring on this or on this, Abd al-Razzaq said: For his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"1020","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Hashim al-Qasim ibn Kathir, from Qays al-Kharifi, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went ahead, Abu Bakr prayed, Umar came third, may Allah be pleased with him, then tribulation struck us, or befell us, so what Allah, Majestic is His majesty, willed, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: His saying, then tribulation struck us, he intended to humble himself thereby."
"1021","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shubah and Hammad ibn Salamah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, that a man asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the cow, and he said: For seven, he said: The horn, he said: It does not harm you, he said: The lame, he said: If it reaches the place of sacrifice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear."
"1022","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Hujayyah ibn Adi, who said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and a man asked him, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1023","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: There was no horseman among us on the day of Badr except al-Miqdad, and I saw us, none among us but asleep, except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under a tree praying and weeping until morning."
"1024","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Husayn, from Umayr ibn Said, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: There is no man on whom I carried out a hadd punishment and he died that I feel regret in myself, except for wine, for had he died I would have paid blood money, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not institute it as a sunnah."
"1025","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution three times."
"1026","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zaidah ibn Qudamah, from Abu Husayn al-Asadi, and Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Husayn al-Asadi informed us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was a man who emitted much madhi, and beneath me was the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I ordered a man and he asked him, and he said: Perform ablution and wash it."
"1027","Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, who said: We prayed Fajr, then we came to him and sat with him, and he called for ablution water, and a vessel with water and a basin were brought, he said: He poured the vessel over his right hand, washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, blew his nose three times with handful after handful, then washed his face three times and his forearms three times three times, then put his hand in the vessel and wiped his head with both hands together one time, then washed his feet thoroughly three times, then said: This is the ablution of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so learn it."
"1028","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was a man who emitted much madhi, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If you see madhi, perform ablution and wash your private part, and if you see the spurting of water, wash fully, and I mentioned it to Sufyan, and he said: I heard it from Rukayn."
"1029","Muawiyah and Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Zaidah narrated to us, al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it, and they said: The spurting of water, and Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, and he said: Spurting also."
"1030","Abd Allah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to me, Khalid informed us, from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, then the best after Abu Bakr is Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, then Allah places good where He loves."
"1031","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Wahid al-Basri narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said when he finished with the people of Basrah: The best of this ummah after its Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Abu Bakr, and after Abu Bakr is Umar, and we have introduced new matters, Allah will do therein what He wills."
"1032","Abd Allah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me, Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Husayn, from al-Musayyab ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Abu Bakr and Umar, and we have introduced after new matters, Allah will decree therein what He wills."
"1033","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ammar came seeking permission to see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Give him permission, welcome to the pure, the purified."
"1034","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Dhi Huddan, one who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called war deception."
"1035","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, my father informed me that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who approaches a woman and emits madhi, for I am shy before him because his daughter is with me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He washes his private part and his testicles and performs ablution."
"1036","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: They distracted us on the day of al-Ahzab from Asr prayer, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They distracted us from the middle prayer, Asr prayer, may Allah fill their graves and their houses, or their bellies, with fire."
"1037","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We have nothing except the Book of Allah, exalted is He, and this sheet from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Madinah is sacred, between Air and Thawr, whoever introduces therein an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, neither just recompense nor ransom is accepted from him, and he said: The protection of the Muslims is one, so whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, neither ransom nor just recompense is accepted from him, and whoever allies with a people without permission of his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, Allah accepts from him neither ransom nor just recompense."
"1038","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you meticulous regarding Quraysh and leave us, that you marry among us, he said: And do you have anything, he said: I said: The daughter of Hamzah, he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."
"1039","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali said: If I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, think of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the most proper, most guided, and most God-fearing."
"1040","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shubah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this ummah after its Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, then Umar."
"1041","Abd Allah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, regarding His saying: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warner, and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim."
"1042","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, who said: When fighting intensified on the day of Badr, we sought protection with the Messenger of Allah, and he was among the strongest of people, there was none closer to the polytheists than him."
"1043","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, from Nafi, and Ishaq, meaning Ibn Isa, narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Hunayn, Ishaq said: From his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing al-qassi and safflower-dyed garments, gold rings, and reciting the Quran in bowing."
"1044","Abd Allah narrated to us, my father and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, they said: Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibrahim ibn Fulan ibn Hunayn, from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn Hunayn, who said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me safflower-dyed garments, al-qassi, gold rings, and reciting in bowing, Ayyub said: Or he said: That I recite while bowing, Abu Khaythamah said in his hadith: I was told that Ismail retracted from: His grandfather Hunayn."
"1045","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from a man, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sell two slave brothers, so I sold them and separated them, and I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Catch them, take them back, do not sell them except together, and do not separate them."
"1046","Abd Allah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah, who said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution, he washed his hands until he cleaned them, then rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped his head, washed his feet to the ankles, took the remainder of his purification water and drank while standing, then said: I wanted to show you how the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was."
"1047","Abd Allah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: Abd Khayr mentioned from Ali the like of the hadith of Abu Hayyah, except that Abd Khayr said: When he finished his purification, he took with his hands from the remainder of his purification water and drank."
"1048","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Said was asked about the animal with broken horn, can it be sacrificed, so he informed us, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, a man from his people, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing an animal with broken horn and ear, Qatadah said: I mentioned that to Said ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: Breaking is half or more than that."
"1049","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, wearing al-qassi, and silk saddle covers."
"1050","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah al-Wadii, Abd al-Razzaq said: From Abu Hayyah, who said: I saw Ali urinate in al-Rahbah, call for water, perform ablution, wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth and sniff water three times, wash his face three times, wash his forearms three times three times, wipe his head, wash his feet three times three times, then stand and drink from the remainder of his ablution, then say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do, and I wanted to show you."
"1051","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to me, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, who said: Alqamah ibn Qays struck this minbar and said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us on this minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, mentioned what Allah willed him to mention, and said: The best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Abu Bakr, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, then we introduced after them matters, Allah will decree therein."
"1052","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, Yunus ibn Khabbab informed me, from al-Musayyab ibn Abd Khayr, from Abd Khayr, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1053","Waki narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Ansari, from Ali, and al-Masudi narrated from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither short nor tall, large of head and beard, coarse of hands and feet, large of joints, his face tinged with redness, long of the masrubah, when he walked he leaned forward as if tearing himself from rock, I never saw before him nor after him his like, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu al-Nadr said: Al-masrubah, and said: As if descending from a slope, and Abu Qatan said: Al-masrubah, and Yazid said: Al-masrubah."
"1054","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I used to think Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith, I said: No, by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not think anyone from the Muslims after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was better than you, he said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I said: Yes, and he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr, I said: Yes, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1055","Abd Allah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Sila informed us, from Abd Khayr, who said: I heard him say: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood on the minbar, mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, succeeded, acted by his practice and followed his way until Allah, mighty and majestic is He, took him in that state, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, succeeded in that manner, acted by their practice and followed their way until Allah, mighty and majestic is He, took him in that state."
"1056","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabiah, who said: I was riding behind Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: In the name of Allah, and when he settled he said: Praise be to Allah, glory be to Him who subjected this to us, and we could not have subdued it, and to our Lord we shall return, and Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, said: Then he praised Allah three times and Allah is Greatest three times, then said: Glory be to Allah three times, then said: There is no god but You, then he returned to the hadith of Waki: Glory be to You, I wronged myself, so forgive me, none forgives sins but You, then he laughed, I said: What makes you laugh, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did as you saw me do, then he laughed, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh, he said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, said: Wonder at My servant, he knows none forgives sins but Me."
"1057","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I complained, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I said: O Allah, if my term has come, relieve me, if it is delayed, heal me or grant me health, and if it is a trial, make me patient, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you say, he said: So I repeated to him, he said: So he wiped with his hand, then said: O Allah, heal him or grant him health, he said: So I never complained of that pain after."
"1058","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten."
"1059","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sila, from Abd Khayr, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Allah took His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the best manner He took a prophet from the prophets, upon them be peace, then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, succeeded, acted by the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the sunnah of His Prophet, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, likewise."
"1060","Abd Allah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us, Umar ibn Mujashi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say on the minbar: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and had I wished to name the third I would have named him, and a man said to Abu Ishaq: They say you say: Best in evil, and he said: Are you a Haruri."
"1061","Waki narrated to us, from Israil and Ali ibn Salih, from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Numan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear, and not to sacrifice a sharqa, kharqa, muqabalah, or mudabarah."
"1062","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me that none loves you but a believer, and none hates you but a hypocrite."
"1063","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash al-Kinani, that a people in Yemen dug a pit for a lion, and it fell in, and people crowded over it, and a man fell in and caught another, then the other caught another, until they were four in it, and they disputed about that until some took arms against others, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to them: Will you kill two hundred for four, but I shall judge among you with a judgment, if you accept it: For the first a quarter of blood money, for the second a third of blood money, for the third half of blood money, and for the fourth full blood money, and they did not accept his judgment, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I shall judge among you with a judgment, he said: So he was informed of the judgment of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he upheld it."
"1064","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Abu Wail, from Abu al-Hayyaj, who said: Ali said to me, and Abd al-Rahman said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Abu al-Hayyaj: I send you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me: That you leave no elevated grave except you level it, nor any image except you efface it."
"1065","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No obedience to a human in disobedience to Allah."
"1066","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb narrate from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking of the ear and horn, he said: So I asked Said ibn al-Musayyab: What is breaking, and he said: Half or more than that."
"1067","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with a funeral in Baqi al-Gharqad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, sat, and we sat around him, and with him was a small stick with which he prodded, then he raised his sight and said: There is no soul breathed among you but its seat in Paradise and Hell is written, already written wretched or happy, and the people said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not rest upon our Book and leave action, for whoever is among the people of happiness will end to happiness, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will end to wretchedness, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather act, for each is facilitated, as for whoever is among the people of wretchedness, he is facilitated to the work of wretchedness, and as for whoever is among the people of happiness, he is facilitated to the work of happiness, then he recited: As for he who gives and fears, to His saying: We shall facilitate him to hardship."
"1068","Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with a funeral in Baqi al-Gharqad, and he mentioned its meaning."
"1069","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb al-Hamdani narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast the day of Ashura and command it."
"1070","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever lies about his two eyes will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to tie a knot between the two ends of a barley grain."
"1071","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath al-Basri narrated to me, and Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Umar and Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I was a man who emitted much madhi, and I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because his daughter was with me, so I ordered a man and he asked him, and he said: From it is ablution."
"1072","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is ablution, its inviolability is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim."
"1073","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shubah, from Mansur, from Hilal, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not pray after Asr except that you pray while the sun is high."
"1074","Abd Allah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, and Ismail Abu Mamar and Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, Abu Mamar said: Freedman of Quraysh, he said: al-Suddi informed me, and Rahmawayh said in his hadith, he said: I heard al-Suddi, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old uncle has died, he said: Go bury him, and do not innovate anything in his affair until you come to me, so I buried him, then I came to him, and he said: Go wash fully, and do not innovate anything until you come to me, so I washed, then I came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications, nothing of red or black camels would delight me as they do, and Ibn Bakkar said in his hadith, al-Suddi said: And Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he washed a dead person, would wash fully."
"1075","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
"1076","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not pray after Asr except that you pray while the sun is high, Sufyan said: I do not know, in Makkah he meant or elsewhere."
"1077","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Ukaydir of Dumah gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a silk suit or a silk garment, he said: So he gave it to me and said: Tear it into headscarves among the women."
"1078","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abd Allah ibn Sabu, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: This will be dyed from this, so what does the most wretched await me, they said: O Commander of the Faithful, inform us of him, we shall destroy his kin, he said: Then by Allah you will kill for me other than my killer, they said: Then appoint a successor over us, he said: No, but I leave you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you to, they said: Then what will you say to your Lord when you come to Him, and Waki once said: When you meet Him, he said: I say: O Allah, You left me among them as long as You willed, then You took me to You while You are among them, if You will You rectify them, and if You will You corrupt them."
"1079","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ammar came and sought permission, and he said: Give him permission, welcome to the pure, the purified."
"1080","Abd Allah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: If you are told from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, think of him as the most proper, the most guided, and the most God-fearing."
"1081","Abd Allah narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of it."
"1082","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: If you are told from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, think of him as the most guided, the most God-fearing, and the most proper."
"1083","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to me, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Abu Marthad and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, and all of us were horsemen, and he said: Go until you come to Rawdat Khakh, so said Ibn Abi Shaybah: Khakh, and Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: Rawdah such and such, and Affan narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn the like of it, he said: Rawdat Khakh."
"1084","Waki narrated to us, Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Umayr ibn Said, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I would never carry out a hadd on a man and he dies and feel regret for it, except the owner of wine, for had he died I would have paid blood money, and Sufyan added: And that is because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not institute it as a sunnah."
"1085","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists, so I said: Do you seek forgiveness for your parents while they are polytheists, and he said: Did not Ibrahim seek forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist, he said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was revealed: It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, to the end of the two verses, Abd al-Rahman said: So Allah revealed: And the seeking of forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father was only due to a promise he had promised him."
"1086","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman narrated from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, falling from the sky is dearer to me than lying upon him, and if I narrate to you between me and you, for war is deception, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall come out a people in the end of time, young in age, foolish, and Abd al-Rahman said: Deficient in understanding, speaking from the speech of the best of creation, reciting the Quran, it does not pass their throats, Abd al-Rahman said: Their faith does not pass their throats, passing through religion as the arrow passes through the game, so if you meet them, kill them, for in killing them is reward for whoever kills them with Allah, mighty and majestic is He, on the Day of Resurrection, Abd al-Rahman said: So if you meet them, kill them, for killing them is reward for whoever kills them on the Day of Resurrection."
"1087","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Israil, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: And you make your provision, he said: Your gratitude, that you deny, he said: You say: We were rained by such and such star."
"1088","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to me, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I think he raised it, he said: Whoever lies in his dream will be charged with tying a barley grain on the Day of Resurrection."
"1089","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri al-Bahili narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever lies in a vision deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
"1090","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Sad ibn Ubaydah narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and al-Zubayr and Abu Marthad, and all of us were horsemen, and he said: Go until you reach Rawdat Khakh, so said Abu Awanah: For therein is a woman with a letter from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to the polytheists, and he mentioned the hadith at length."
"1091","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed debt before bequest, while you recite: After a bequest bequeathed or debt, and full brothers inherit to the exclusion of half-brothers by the father."
"1092","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali said: If you are told from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, think of him as the most proper, the most guided, and the most God-fearing."
"1093","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Najiyah ibn Kab, from Ali, who said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old erring uncle has died, and he said: Go bury him, and do not innovate anything until you come to me, he said: So I went and buried him, and he ordered me and I washed fully, then he supplicated for me with supplications, I would not love to have instead of them all worldly goods."
"1094","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Masud ibn al-Hakam, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for a funeral, so we stood, then he sat, so we sat."
"1095","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No obedience to a creature in disobedience to Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"1096","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Ali said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not point you to the most beautiful girl in Quraysh, he said: Who is she, I said: The daughter of Hamzah, he said: Do you not know she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding, Allah forbade through breastfeeding what He forbade through lineage."
"1097","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have pardoned you the charity of horses and slaves, but bring a quarter of a tenth, from every forty dirhams a dirham."
"1098","Waki and Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, they said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Waki said: He said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Hunayn, and Uthman said: From Abd Allah ibn Hunayn: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me, and I do not say he forbade you, safflower-dyed garments and gold rings."
"1099","Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to me, my father narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you meticulous regarding Quraysh and leave us, he said: Do you have anything, I said: The daughter of Hamzah, he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."
"1100","Waki narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman al-Makki narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he slaughtered the camels, ordered me to give in charity their meat, their skins, and their coverings."
"1101","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Abd al-Rahman added, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me not to give the butcher anything from it in payment for his slaughtering."
"1102","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the gold ring, and the mitharah, and the qassi, and the ji'ah."
"1103","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, he said: When the ten entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake his family and lift the izar. It was said to Abu Bakr: What is lifting the izar? He said: He kept away from women."
"1104","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shu'bah and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten of Ramadan."
"1105","Abdullah narrated to us, Yusuf al-Saffar the freedman of Banu Umayyah and Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to me, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, he said: When the last ten entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would tighten the izar and wake his women. Ibn Waki' said: He lifted the izar."
"1106","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar the freedman of Banu Hashim narrated to me, Abu Waki' al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear thoroughly and above."
"1107","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Hashim ibn Kathir, from Qays al-Kharifi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went ahead, and Abu Bakr prayed, and Umar was third, then fitnah struck us, and it is as Allah wills."
"1108","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman al-Thaqafi, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to breed a donkey onto a horse."
"1109","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of its women is Khadijah, and the best of its women is Maryam bint Imran."
"1110","Waki': al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, I think he said at Baqi' al-Gharqad, he said: He scratched in the ground, then raised his head and said: There is none among you but his seat in Paradise and his seat in Hell has been written. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not then rely? He said: No, act, for each is facilitated. Then he recited: As for him who gives and fears, up to His saying: We shall facilitate for him the difficult path."
"1111","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to me, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan, and if you are overcome, then do not be overcome regarding the remaining seven."
"1112","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from a man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant will not believe until he believes in four: he believes in Allah, and that Allah sent me with the truth, and he believes in the resurrection after death, and he believes in qadar, its good and its evil."
"1113","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed me, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring, and wearing qassi, and the mitharah."
"1114","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights and lift the izar."
"1115","Abdullah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Shu'bah and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the ten."
"1116","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, he said: We were with Ali, and he called a son of his called Uthman, who had a forelock."
"1117","Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: My father used to spend the evening conversing with Ali, and Ali would wear summer clothes in winter and winter clothes in summer. It was said to him: Why do you not ask him? So he asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me when I had ophthalmia on the day of Khaybar, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have ophthalmia, so he spat in my eye and said: O Allah, remove from him heat and cold. So I have felt neither heat nor cold since. He said: And he said: I shall send a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, and who loves Allah and His Messenger, who is not a fleer. He said: The people craned their necks for it. He said: So he sent Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1118","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu al-Sari Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, and Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Ali ibn Hakim said in his hadith: Are you not jealous that your women go out? And Hannad said in his hadith: Are you not ashamed, or are you not jealous? For it has reached me that your women go out in the markets crowding the non-Arabs."
"1119","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah narrating from Shurayh ibn Hani', that he asked A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about wiping over the khuffs, and she said: Ask about that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, for he used to go on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he asked him, and he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. It was said to Muhammad: Did he raise it to the Prophet? He said: He considered it raised, but he was in awe of it."
"1120","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver and its scribe and its witness, and the tattooer and the one tattooed. Ibn Awn said: I said: Except for a disease? He said: Yes. And the muhallil and the one for whom it is done, and the withholder of charity. And he said: He used to forbid wailing, and he did not say: He cursed. So I said: Who narrated to you? He said: al-Harith al-A'war al-Hamdani."
"1121","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji and Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Imran al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, and this is the wording of Muhammad ibn Aban, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a spot of a hair from janabah untouched by water, such-and-such of Hell will be done to him. Ali said: So from then I became hostile to my hair, as you see."
"1122","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Umayr, Sharik said: I said to him: From whom, O Abu Umayr, from whom did he narrate it? He said: From Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large-headed, with redness mixed in his complexion, thick in the palms and feet, large-bearded, long in the line of hair on the chest, large in the joints, walking on a slope, leaning forward in gait, neither short nor tall. I never saw anyone like him before him nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1123","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the Quran as long as he was not junub."
"1124","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi informed us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, he said: I was sitting with my father when Ali came, so he stood over us and greeted, then ordered Abu Musa with some matters of the people. He said: Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Ask Allah for guidance, meaning thereby guidance of the road, and ask Allah for soundness, meaning thereby your straightening the arrow. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to place my ring on this or this, the forefinger and the middle. He said: He was standing, so I do not know which of the two he meant. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the mitharah and the qassiyyah. We said to him: O Commander of the Believers, what is the mitharah? He said: Something women make for their husbands on their saddles. He said: We said: What is the qassiyyah? He said: Garments that come to us from Syria, striped, with patterns like citrons. He said: Abu Burdah said: When I saw al-sabani I knew it was that."
"1125","Abdullah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Maysarah and Zadhan, they said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, drank standing, then said: If I drink standing, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing, and if I drink sitting, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink sitting."
"1126","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"1127","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith, for me to fall from the sky to the earth is dearer to me than to say about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say, but war is deceit."
"1128","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, that Ali ibn Abi Talib drank standing, and the people looked and disapproved of that, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What are you looking at? If I drink standing, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing, and if I drink sitting, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink sitting."
"1129","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Warqa' informed me, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"1130","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: and Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and he commanded me, so I gave the cupper his wage."
"1131","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from Zadhan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Khadijah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about two sons of hers who died in Jahiliyyah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are in Hell. He said: When he saw dislike in her face, he said: Had you seen their place you would have hated them. She said: O Messenger of Allah, then my son from you? He said: In Paradise. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers and their children are in Paradise, and the polytheists and their children are in Hell. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And those who believed and their offspring followed them in faith, We shall join their offspring to them."
"1132","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on the day of al-Khandaq at a gap of the trench gaps, and said: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their bellies and their houses with fire."
"1133","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, Abd Khayr narrated to us, he said: Ali sat after he prayed Fajr in al-Rahbah, then said to his boy: Bring me water for purification. So the boy brought him a vessel with water and a basin. Abd Khayr said: And we were sitting looking at him. So he took the vessel with his right and poured it onto his left hand, then washed his palms, then took the vessel with his right hand and poured onto his left hand, then washed his palms, doing that three times. Abd Khayr said: Each time he did not insert his hand into the vessel until he had washed it three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and blew it out with his left hand, doing that three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel and washed his face three times. Then he washed his right hand three times to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times to the elbow. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel until the water covered it, then raised it with what it carried of water, then wiped it with his left hand, then wiped his head with both his hands once. Then he poured with his right hand three times onto his right foot, then washed it with his left hand. Then he poured with his right hand onto his left foot, then washed it with his left hand three times. Then he inserted his right hand and scooped with his palm and drank. Then he said: This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is his purification."
"1134","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Ahzab: O Allah, fill their houses and their graves with fire, as they distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set."
"1135","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Mujahid, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was once severely hungry in Madinah, so I went out seeking work in the outskirts of Madinah, and there was a woman who had gathered mud, and I thought she wanted to wet it, so I came to her and contracted with her for a date for each bucket, so I drew sixteen buckets until my hands blistered, then I went to the water and took some from it, then I came to her and said with my palms like this before her, and Isma'il spread his hands and joined them, so she counted out sixteen dates for me, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he ate some of them with me."
"1136","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, and Abdullah narrated to us, he said: and Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Abu Jamilah al-Tuhawi, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, then said to the cupper when he finished: How much is your fee? He said: Two sa's. So he remitted one sa' from him, and commanded me, so I gave him one sa'."
"1137","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Abdullah narrated to us, he said: and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that a servant girl of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed fornication, so he commanded me to carry out the hadd on her, but I found her not yet dried of her blood, so I came to him and mentioned that to him, and he said: When she is dried of her blood, carry out the hadd on her. Carry out the hudud on those your right hands possess. And this is the wording of the hadith of Ishaq ibn Isma'il."
"1138","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to me, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of a slave girl of his who had committed fornication, then he mentioned the hadith."
"1139","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, that he said: I witnessed Ali and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, between Makkah and Madinah, with Uthman forbidding mut'ah and combining the two, and when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saw that, he entered ihram for both, saying: Labbayk with umrah and hajj together. So Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do you see me forbidding the people from it while you do it? He said: I would not leave the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the word of any of the people."
"1140","Abdullah narrated to us, my father and Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to me, they said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, and Abdullah narrated to us, he said: and Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to me, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, all from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Maysarah: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, drink standing, so I said: Do you drink while standing? He said: If I drink standing, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing, and if I drink sitting, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink sitting."
"1141","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, Ali narrated to us, that Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, complained of what she suffered from the trace of the millstone on her hand, and captives came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she went but did not find him, and met A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and informed her. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, A'ishah informed him of the coming of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, to her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came when we had taken our beds, and we went to rise, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In your places. So he sat between us until I felt the coolness of his feet on my chest, and said: Shall I not teach you better than what you asked? When you take your beds, magnify Allah thirty-four times, and glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times, for it is better for you than a servant."
"1142","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar the freedman of Banu Hashim and Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to me, they said: Abu Waki' al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abu al-Rabi' said in his hadith: from Maysarah Abu Jamilah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a black slave girl of his who had committed fornication, to flog her the hadd. He said: I found her in her blood, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, and he said to me: When she recovers from her postpartum, flog her fifty. And Abu al-Rabi' said in his hadith, he said: I informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When she is dried of her blood, carry out the hadd on her. Then he said: Carry out the hudud."
"1143","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would travel until when the sun set and it darkened, he dismounted and prayed Maghrib, then prayed Isha right after it, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"1144","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to them, that Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, complained to her father of what her hands suffered from the millstone, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Shu'bah."
"1145","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari al-Ta'i, he said: One who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, I said: You send me when I am a young man with no knowledge of much judgment. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck my chest and said: Go, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will steady your tongue and guide your heart. He said: No judgment between two men has since eluded me."
"1146","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Ali and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, met at Usfan, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, would forbid mut'ah and umrah. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What do you intend by forbidding a matter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did? So Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Leave us alone from you."
"1147","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaddad say: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) join his parents for anyone except Sa'd ibn Malik, for on the day of Uhud he kept saying: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"1148","Abdullah narrated to us, my father and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to me, they said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, and Abdullah narrated to us, he said: and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Abd al-Samad and Mu'adh narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu al-Aswad, and Abu Khaythamah said in his hadith: Ibn Abi al-Aswad, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The urine of a suckling boy is sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is washed. Qatadah said: And this is as long as they have not tasted food; when they have tasted food, both are washed. Abdullah said: And Abu Khaythamah did not mention in his hadith the saying of Qatadah."
"1149","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the suckling: The urine of the boy is sprinkled, and the urine of the girl is washed. Qatadah said: And this is as long as they have not tasted food; when they have tasted, both are washed."
"1150","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Ahzab: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their graves with fire, or their houses, or their bellies. Shu'bah doubted regarding the houses and the bellies."
"1151","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Hassan narrating from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Ahzab: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their graves and their houses, or their bellies, with fire. He doubted regarding the houses and the bellies; as for the graves, there is no doubt in it."
"1152","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr in every part of the night, its beginning and its middle and its end, and his witr ended at its end."
"1153","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten of Ramadan."
"1154","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that a silk robe was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he clothed me with it. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I went out in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself. He said: So he commanded me, and I split it among my women as headcovers, between Fatimah and his aunt."
"1155","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to me, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Utaybah, and he is al-Darir, narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Asram, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, he left a dinar and a dirham. So he said: Two brands. Pray over your companion."
"1156","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, then he mentioned the like of it, similar."
"1157","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb say: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking the horn and the ear. Qatadah said: So I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I said: What is breaking the ear? He said: When it is half or more than that."
"1158","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing with a broken horn or ear. Qatadah said: So I mentioned that to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: Yes, the break is half or more than that."
"1159","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or he forbade me, the mitharah and the qassi and the gold ring."
"1160","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Ammar sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The good, the perfumed. Admit him."
"1161","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Mudarrib narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: You saw us on the night of Badr, and there was none among us but asleep, except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he was praying toward a tree and supplicating until morning. And there was no horseman among us on the day of Badr except al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad."
"1162","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, he said: Zayd ibn Suhan came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Narrate to me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you. He said: He forbade me the hantam and the dubba' and the naqir and the ji'ah, and the gold ring, or he said: the gold circle, and silk, and qassi, and the red mitharah. He said: And a silk robe was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he clothed me with it, and I went out in it, so he took it and gave it to Fatimah, or his aunt. Isma'il says that."
"1163","Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, then he mentioned it with its isnad and meaning, except that he said: Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1164","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Dirar ibn Murrah, from Husayn al-Muzani, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said on the minbar: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nothing cuts off prayer except hadath. I am not ashamed to tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not ashamed of. He said: And hadath is to break wind audibly or silently."
"1165","Abdullah narrated to us, Qatan ibn Nusayr Abu Abbad al-Dhari' narrated to me, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Utaybah al-Darir narrated to us, Burayd ibn Asram narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, leaving a dinar and a dirham, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, he left a dinar and a dirham. So he said: Two brands. Pray over your companion."
"1166","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Salamah, meaning Ibn Abi al-Husam, narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from a man of the Ansar, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person walks in the harvest of Paradise, and when he sits with him he is immersed in mercy, and when he leaves him, seventy thousand angels are charged with him seeking forgiveness for him that day."
"1167","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed us, Shu'bah informed us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Hajjaj said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand for a funeral, so we stood, and I saw him sit, so we sat."
"1168","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: I heard Abu Burdah, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance and soundness, and recall with guidance Your guiding the road, and recall with soundness your straightening the arrow. He said: And he forbade, or forbade me, qassi and mitharah, and the ring on the forefinger or the middle."
"1169","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Awn, he said: I heard Abu Salih, he said: Ali said: I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"1170","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Mubaraki Sulayman ibn Muhammad narrated to me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Muwarri', from Ali, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, and he said: Who will go to Madinah and leave no grave but level it, and no image but efface it, and no idol but break it? He said: A man stood and said: I will. Then he feared the people of Madinah and sat. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I went, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I left no grave in Madinah but leveled it, and no image but effaced it, and no idol but broke it. He said: He said: Whoever returns and does any of that has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad. O Ali, do not be a tempter, or he said: conceited, nor a trader except a trader in good, for those are the procrastinators in deeds."
"1171","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A striped silk robe was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent it to me. So I went out in it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until I saw anger in his face, and said: I did not give it to you to wear. He said: So he commanded me, and I tore it among my women."
"1172","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, nor a junub, nor a dog."
"1173","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, that he witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, pray Zuhr, then sit in al-Rahbah for the needs of the people. When Asr came, a basin was brought, so he took a handful of water and wiped his hands and forearms and face and head and feet, then drank its remainder standing, then said: Some people dislike drinking while standing, yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did as I did. And this is the wudu of one who has not broken wudu."
"1174","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah informed us, he said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: A jug was brought."
"1175","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed me, from Abu Muhammad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Madinah and commanded him to level the graves."
"1176","Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to me, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abu Muhammad al-Hudhali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of the Ansar to level every grave and to smear every idol. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I dislike entering the houses of my people. He said: So he sent me, and when I came, he said: O Ali, do not be a tempter, nor conceited, nor a trader except a trader in good, for those are procrastinating, or outstripped, in deeds."
"1177","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from a man of the people of Basrah, he said: And the people of Basrah kunya him Abu Muwarri', he said: And the people of Kufah kunya him Abu Muhammad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at a funeral, then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Abu Dawud from Abu Shihab."
"1178","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Malik ibn Urfatah, he said: I heard Abd Khayr, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, brought a chair, so he sat on it, then a jug was brought. Hajjaj said: A basin of water. He said: So he washed his hands three times, and rinsed his mouth three times with sniffing with one water, and washed his face three times, and washed his forearms three times. Hajjaj said: Three times three times with one hand. And he put his hands in the basin, then wiped his head. Hajjaj said: He motioned with his hands from the front of his head to the back of his head. He said: And I do not know whether he returned them to the front of his head or not. And he washed his feet three times. Hajjaj said: Three times three times. Then he said: Whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1179","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Jamil ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi', he said: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, where he killed the people of al-Nahrawan. He said: Seek for me al-Mukhda. So they sought him among the slain and said: We do not find him. He said: Return and seek. By Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to. So they returned and sought him, repeating that several times, each time swearing by Allah: I did not lie nor was I lied to. So they went and found him under the slain in mud, and brought him out and brought him. Abu al-Wadi' said: It is as if I look at him, an Abyssinian with a teat that had covered one of his hands, like the breast of a woman, with hairs on it like hairs on the tail of a jerboa."
"1180","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba' and the muzaffat."
"1181","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was at a funeral and took a stick scratching in the ground and said: There is none among you but his seat in Hell or in Paradise has been written. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not then rely? He said: Act, for each is facilitated. As for him who gives and fears and confirms the best, We shall facilitate for him ease. And as for him who withholds and deems himself rich and denies the best, We shall facilitate for him hardship. Shu'bah said: And Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated it to me, and I did not deny anything of the hadith of Sulayman."
"1182","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman narrating from al-Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was shy to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhi because of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, so I ordered al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, and he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: In it is wudu."
"1183","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wanted to stone a madwoman, so Ali said to him: You have no right to that. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he dreams, and from the madman until he recovers or regains reason. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, averted it from her."
"1184","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Danaj, from Hudayn, he said: Testimony was given against al-Walid ibn Uqbah before Uthman that he drank wine, so Ali spoke to Uthman about him, and he said: You deal with your cousin, flog him. He said: Rise, O Hasan. He said: What is yours and this? Let another than you take charge of this. He said: Rather you are incapable and weak and feeble. Rise, O Abdullah ibn Ja'far. So he flogged him, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, counted. When he completed forty, he said: Enough, or: Stop. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged forty, and Abu Bakr forty, and Umar completed it eighty, and each is sunnah."
"1185","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, that Sharahah al-Hamdaniyyah came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I committed fornication. He said: Perhaps you are other than pregnant, perhaps you saw in your dream, perhaps you were coerced. Each she said: No. So he flogged her on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and said: I flogged her by the Book of Allah, and stoned her by the sunnah of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1186","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Abu Ubayd the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that anyone keep any of his sacrifice beyond three days."
"1187","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb and Sufyan ibn Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to me, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Nu'aym ibn Dijajah al-Asadi, he said: I was with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when Abu Mas'ud entered upon him and said to him: O Farrukh, are you the one who says: A hundred years will not come upon the people while an eye blinks on earth? Your buttocks have missed the hole. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: A hundred years will not come upon the people while an eye blinks on earth of those alive today. Relief of this and its ease is after the hundred."
"1188","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Jamil ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi', he said: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he killed the people of al-Nahrawan. He said: Seek al-Mukhda among the slain. They said: We did not find him. He said: Seek him. By Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to. Until they brought him out from under the slain. Abu al-Wadi' said: It is as if I look at him, an Abyssinian, one of his hands like the breast of a woman, with hairs on it like the tail of a jerboa."
"1189","Abdullah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Sha'ir narrated to me, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, that Abu al-Wadi' Abbad narrated to him, that he said: We were heading to Kufah with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and when we reached two or three nights journey from Harura', many people broke away from us, so we mentioned that to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Let not their affair frighten you, for they will return. Then he mentioned the hadith at length. He said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, praised Allah and said: My close friend informed me that the leader of these is a man defective in the hand, with hairs on the nipple of his teat as if they were the tail of a jerboa. So seek him, but they did not find him. So we came to him and said: We did not find him. He said: Seek him. By Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to, three times. So we said: We did not find him. So Ali came himself and kept saying: Turn this, turn this, until a man of Kufah came and said: Here he is. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah is Greatest. No one will come to you informing you of his father. The people kept saying: This is a king, this is a king. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Whose son is he?"
"1190","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Sharahah: Perhaps you were coerced, perhaps your husband came to you, perhaps, perhaps. She said: No. He said: When she delivered what was in her belly, he flogged her, then stoned her. It was said to him: You flogged her then stoned her. He said: I flogged her by the Book of Allah, and stoned her by the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1191","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Habbah al-Urani, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I am the first man who prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1192","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, from Shu'bah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Habbah al-Urani, he said: I heard Ali say: I am the first who prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1193","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: Then I witnessed it with Ali, and he prayed before he preached, without adhan or iqamah, then preached and said: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you to eat your sacrifices after three nights, so do not eat them after."
"1194","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not pray after Asr unless you pray while the sun is high."
"1195","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast continuously from suhur to suhur."
"1196","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Ali, he said: Some people came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, complaining of the collectors of Uthman. He said: My father said to me: Go with this letter to Uthman and say to him: The people have complained of your collectors, and this is the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding charity, so order them to take by it. He said: So I came to Uthman and mentioned that to him. He said: Had he mentioned Uthman with anything, he would have mentioned him that day, meaning with evil."
"1197","Abdullah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to me, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to me, Yazid ibn Salih narrated to us, that Abu al-Wadi' Abbad narrated to him, that he said: We were heading to Kufah with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, then he mentioned the hadith of al-Mukhda. Ali said: By Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to, three times. So Ali said: My close friend informed me of three brothers of the jinn, this is the eldest of them, and the second has a large gathering, and the third has weakness in him."
"1198","Abdullah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, he said: We prayed the morning prayer, then sat with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and he called for wudu water, and washed his hands three times, and rinsed his mouth twice from one palm, then washed his face three times, then washed his forearms, then washed his feet three times, then said: This is the wudu of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so know."
"1199","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, he said: We came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he had prayed, and he called for a jug, then rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed three times, rinsing from the palm he takes with, and washed his face three times, and his right hand three times, and his left hand three times, then said: Whoever is pleased to know the wudu of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is it."
"1200","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, he said: We were with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when a funeral passed by him, so some people stood for it. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Who gave you this fatwa? They said: Abu Musa. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only did that once, imitating the People of the Book, and when he was forbidden, he stopped."
"1201","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ali ibn Husayn ibn Ali, from his father Husayn ibn Ali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said, Ali said: I acquired an old she-camel along with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the spoils on the day of Badr, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me another old she-camel, so one day I made them kneel at the door of a man of the Ansar, intending to load idhkhir upon them to sell it, and with me was a goldsmith of Banu Qaynuqa to help me with the wedding feast of Fatimah, while Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib was drinking in that house, so Hamzah sprang upon them with the sword and cut off their humps and ripped open their flanks, then he took from their livers. I said to Ibn Shihab: And from the hump? He said: He cut off their humps and went away with it. He said: So I looked at a sight that horrified me, so I came to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with him was Zayd ibn Harithah, and I informed him of the news, so he went out and with him was Zayd, and he went with him and entered upon Hamzah and expressed anger at him, so Hamzah raised his gaze and said: Are you but slaves of my father? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned retreating until he went out from them, and that was before the prohibition of wine."
"1202","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: Some companions of Ali said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Will you not narrate to us the daytime prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the voluntary prayer? So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, you cannot bear it. So they said to him: Inform us of it; we will take from it what we can. Then he mentioned the hadith at length."
"1203","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, by dictation to me from his book, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was asked about the daytime prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: He used to pray sixteen rakahs. He said: He would pray, when the sun was on this side like its position on this side as the Asr prayer, two rakahs, and he would pray, when the sun was on this side like its position on this side as the Zuhr prayer, four rakahs, and he would pray before Zuhr four rakahs and after Zuhr two rakahs and before Asr four rakahs."
"1204","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan and Abdullah, the two sons of Muhammad ibn Ali, from their father Muhammad ibn Ali, that he heard his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying to Ibn Abbas, when it reached him that he permitted mutah of women: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it on the day of Khaybar, and forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"1205","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he performed ablution three times three times, then he wiped his head, then he drank the remainder of his ablution water, then he said: Whoever wishes to look at the ablution of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, let him look at this."
"1206","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from a shaykh of theirs called Salim, from Abdullah ibn Mulayl, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Every prophet was given seven noble men of his ummah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was given fourteen noble men of his ummah, among them Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"1207","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Ubad, he said: We were with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and whenever he witnessed a battleground or overlooked a hill or descended into a valley, he said: Glory be to Allah; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. So I said to a man of Banu Yashkur: Come with us to the Commander of the Believers until we ask him about his saying: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. He said: So we went to him and said: O Commander of the Believers, we saw you, when you witnessed a battleground or descended into a valley or overlooked a hill, you said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, so did the Messenger of Allah entrust to you anything concerning that? He said: So he turned away from us, and we pressed him, and when he saw that, he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not entrust to me any covenant except something he entrusted to the people, but the people fell upon Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and killed him, so one other than me was in a worse state and deed therein than me, then I saw that I was the most entitled of them to this matter, so I leapt upon it, and Allah knows whether we were right or mistaken."
"1208","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq. Abdullah said: And my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the daytime voluntary prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Ali said: Those are sixteen rakahs, the daytime voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and few persist in it. Waki narrated to us, he said: And my father said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit said: O Abu Ishaq, I would not love to have in exchange for this hadith of yours the full of this mosque of yours in gold."
"1209","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to take charge of his sacrificial camels and to give in charity their skins and their coverings."
"1210","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Mujalid informed us, from Amir, he said: Shurahah became pregnant while her husband was absent, so her master took her to Ali, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to her: Perhaps your husband came to you, or perhaps someone forced you against yourself. She said: No, and she confessed to adultery. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged her on Thursday, I being a witness, and stoned her on Friday, I being a witness. So he ordered that a pit be dug for her up to the navel, then he said: Stoning is a sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the verse of stoning had been revealed, but those who used to recite it, and verses of the Quran, perished at al-Yamamah."
"1211","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two litigants bring their case to you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says; you will see how to judge. He said: So I have remained a judge ever since."
"1212","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, that Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to him that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best of its women is Maryam daughter of Imran, and the best of its women is Khadijah."
"1213","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muadh, meaning al-Sanani, narrated to us, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever wishes that his lifespan be extended for him and his provision be widened for him and an evil death be warded off from him, let him fear Allah and uphold his ties of kinship."
"1214","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Witr and loves the witr, so perform the witr, O people of the Quran."
"1215","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to me, Shubah narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed the witr at every part of the night, at its beginning and its middle and its end, and his witr ended at the end of the night."
"1216","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to us, from a man called Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The sun eclipsed, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed with the people; he recited Ya-Sin or the like, then he bowed for about the length of the chapter, then he raised his head and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he stood for the length of the chapter, supplicating and magnifying Allah, then he bowed for the length of his recitation also, then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he stood also for the length of the chapter, then he bowed for that length also, until he prayed four bowings, then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he prostrated, then he stood in the second rakah and did as he did in the first rakah, then he sat supplicating and beseeching until the sun cleared. Then he informed them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did likewise."
"1217","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray any prayer but that he prayed two rakahs after it."
"1218","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform the witr at the beginning of the night and in its middle and at its end, then the witr became fixed for him at its end."
"1219","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the servant sits in his place of prayer after the prayer, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their invoking blessings upon him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. And if he sits awaiting the prayer, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their invoking blessings upon him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"1220","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The witr is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1221","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of the Trench: What is with them? May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire, as they detained us from the middle prayer until the sun set."
"1222","Yazid narrated to us, Zakariyya informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: You recite: after a bequest he bequeaths or a debt, yet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged the debt before the bequest, and full brothers from the same mother inherit to the exclusion of sons of different mothers; a man inherits from his full brother through his father and mother to the exclusion of his brother through his father."
"1223","Yazid narrated to us, Misar informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: Ali was brought a vessel of water, so he drank while standing, then he said: It has reached me that some people dislike that one of them drinks while standing, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do as I did. Then he took from it and wiped himself, then he said: This is the ablution of one who has not broken his ablution."
"1224","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, he said: Ali said to the people of al-Nahrawan: Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or with a small hand, or with a deficient hand. Were it not that you would become overconfident, I would inform you of what Allah decreed upon the tongue of His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for whoever killed them. Abidah said: So I said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Did you hear it yourself? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, swearing upon it three times."
"1225","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Witr and loves the witr, so perform the witr, O people of the Quran."
"1226","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah al-Saluli, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray two rakahs after every prescribed prayer, except Fajr and Asr."
"1227","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray any prayer after which prayer is performed but that he prayed two rakahs after it."
"1228","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Witr and loves the witr, so perform the witr, O people of the Quran."
"1229","Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us one night until he placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and he taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three glorifications and thirty-three praises and thirty-four magnifications. Ali said: So I have not abandoned it since. So a man said to him: Not even on the night of Siffin? He said: Not even on the night of Siffin."
"1230","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Abdullah al-Danaj, from Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Harith ibn Walah, that al-Walid ibn Uqbah prayed Fajr with the people as four rakahs, then he turned to them and said: Shall I add for you? So that was reported to Uthman, so he ordered that he be flogged. So Ali said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: Stand, O Hasan, and flog him. He said: And what are you doing with that? So Ali said: Rather you are incapable and weak. Stand, O Abdullah ibn Jafar, and flog him. So Abdullah ibn Jafar stood and flogged him while Ali counted, and when he reached forty, he said to him: Stop. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck forty for wine, and Abu Bakr struck forty, and Umar struck in the early part of his caliphate, then Umar completed it as eighty, and each is a sunnah."
"1231","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said informed us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that a slave girl of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave birth following adultery, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to carry out the prescribed punishment upon her, so I found her with blood not yet dried from her, so I returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. So he said to me: When the blood dries from her, flog her the prescribed punishment. Then he said: Carry out the prescribed punishments upon those whom your right hands possess."
"1232","Abdullah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The witr is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so perform the witr, O people of the Quran."
"1233","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have exempted you from charity on horses and slaves, so pay the charity on silver: from every forty dirhams a dirham, and in ninety and one hundred there is nothing, and when it reaches two hundred, therein are five dirhams."
"1234","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He used to pray sixteen rakahs at night."
"1235","Yazid narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus informed us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Khosrau gave a gift to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he accepted from him, and Caesar gave a gift to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he accepted from him, and kings gave gifts and he accepted from them."
"1236","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Rabiah ibn al-Nabighah, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade visiting graves and forbade vessels and that the meat of sacrifices be kept beyond three days, then he said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, for they remind you of the Hereafter, and I had forbidden you regarding vessels, so drink in them but avoid everything intoxicating, and I had forbidden you from keeping the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, so keep what seems good to you."
"1237","Affan narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Rabiah ibn al-Nabighah, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade visiting graves, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: And beware of every intoxicant."
"1238","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ali, he said: I was a man who emitted much madhiy, so I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, because of his daughter, so I ordered al-Miqdad, and he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a man who finds madhiy. So he said: That is the water of the stallion, and every stallion has water, so let him wash his private part and his testicles and perform ablution as for prayer."
"1239","Yazid narrated to us, Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Ibn Ashwa, from Hanash ibn al-Mutamir, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sent his chief of police and said: I send you with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me with: Do not leave any grave but that you level it, nor any statue but that you put it down."
"1240","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For what the sky waters, therein is a tenth, and what is watered by the gharb and the daliyah, therein is half a tenth. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: So I narrated to my father the hadith of Uthman from Jarir, and he rejected it, and my father would not narrate to us from Muhammad ibn Salim due to his weakness in his view and his rejection of his hadith."
"1241","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar narrated to me, Abd al-Rahim, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray sixteen rakahs at night besides the prescribed prayer."
"1242","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, Abd al-Rahim al-Razi informed us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah and al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: We came to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not narrate to us about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So he said: And which of you can bear it? They said: We will take from it what we can. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray sixteen rakahs by day besides the prescribed prayer."
"1243","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan and Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I have exempted you from the charity on horses and slaves, so pay a quarter of a tenth."
"1244","Yazid narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus informed us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Ali, I love for you what I love for myself, and I dislike for you what I dislike for myself: Do not recite while bowing nor while prostrating, and do not pray with your hair tied up, for it is the share of Satan, and do not squat between the two prostrations, and do not play with pebbles, and do not spread your forearms, and do not prompt the imam, and do not wear a ring of gold, and do not wear qassi garments, and do not ride upon mayathir."
"1245","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani, he said: I came to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, asking her about leather socks, so she said: Upon you is Ibn Abi Talib; ask him, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I came to him and asked him, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"1246","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl al-Absi, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: When it was the day of al-Ahzab, we prayed Asr between Maghrib and Isha, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer; may Allah fill their graves and their bellies with fire."
"1247","Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Khalid, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me but did not enter upon me, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: What prevented you from entering? He said: We do not enter a house in which there is an image or urine."
"1248","And Abdullah narrated to us, he said: And Shayban narrated it to us another time, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Dhakwan, from Amr ibn Khalid, from Habbah ibn Abi Habbah, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me greeting me, then he mentioned the hadith similarly, like it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And my father would not narrate from Amr ibn Khalid, meaning his hadith was worth nothing in his view."
"1249","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari al-Qurashi narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do not uncover your thigh, and do not look at the thigh of a living one nor a dead one."
"1250","Aswad ibn Amir and Husayn and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said to Fatimah: If you came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him for a servant, for grinding and work have exhausted you. Husayn said: Grinding and work have strained you, and likewise Abu Ahmad said. She said: So go with me. He said: So I went with her, and we asked him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not guide you both to what is better for you than that? When you retire to your beds, glorify Allah thirty-three times and praise Him thirty-three times and magnify Him thirty-four times, for that is one hundred upon the tongue and one thousand in the balance. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have not abandoned it since I heard it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So a man said: Not even on the night of Siffin? He said: Not even on the night of Siffin."
"1251","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: I entered upon Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, and he had prayed Fajr and was sitting in the gathering, so I said: If you stood to your bed, it would be softer for you. So he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prays Fajr then sits in his place of prayer, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their invoking blessings upon him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. And whoever awaits the prayer, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their invoking blessings upon him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"1252","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Duha when the sun was in the east at its position in the west at the time of the Asr prayer."
"1253","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks for something beyond sufficiency, he increases thereby from the embers of Hell. They said: What is beyond sufficiency? He said: A night's supper."
"1254","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Abd al-Samad, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade every predator with fangs of beasts and every bird with talons, and forbade the price of carrion and the flesh of domestic donkeys and the dowry of the prostitute and the stud fee of the stallion and purple mayathir."
"1255","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Ala, from Tariq ibn Ziyad, he said: Ali marched to al-Nahrawan and killed the Khawarij, then he said: Search, for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come a people speaking the word of truth, not passing their throats; they will pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the game; their mark, or among them, is a black man with a deficient arm, on his arm black hairs. If he is among them, then you have killed the worst of people, and if he is not among them, then you have killed the best of people. He said: Then we found the deficient-armed one. He said: So we fell in prostration, and Ali prostrated with us."
"1256","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Sufyan, he said: A man delivered a sermon on the day of Basrah when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prevailed, so Ali said: This is the eloquent preacher. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led, and Abu Bakr prayed second, and Umar was third, then a trial struck us after them; Allah does therein what He wills."
"1257","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali, he said: It was said to Ali and to Abu Bakr on the day of Badr: With one of you is Jibril and with the other is Mikail, and Israfil is a great angel witnessing the fighting, or he said: witnessing the ranks."
"1258","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed four rakahs before Zuhr."
"1259","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Kathir Abu Hashim, seller of sabiri cloth, from Qays al-Kharifi, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying upon this pulpit: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed second, and Umar was third, then a trial struck us, or a trial befell us, so there was what Allah willed."
"1260","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abduwayh Abu Muhammad, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed the witr at every part of the night, at its beginning and its middle and its end, and his witr ended at the end of the night."
"1261","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Said ibn Khuthaym Abu Mamar al-Hilali narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray eight rakahs as voluntary prayer, and by day twelve rakahs."
"1262","Abdullah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sandal and Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, together in the year two hundred and twenty-six, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah al-Saluli, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Indeed the witr is not obligatory like your prescribed prayer, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed the witr, then he said: Perform the witr, O people of the Quran, perform the witr, for Allah is Witr and loves the witr. And this is the wording of the hadith of Abdullah ibn Sandal, and their meaning is one."
"1263","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Nafi al-Nawwa, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mulayl, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was no prophet before me but that he was given seven noble upright companions and ministers, and I was given fourteen: Hamzah and Jafar and Ali and Hasan and Husayn and Abu Bakr and Umar and al-Miqdad and Abdullah ibn Masud and Abu Dharr and Hudhayfah and Salman and Ammar and Bilal."
"1264","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution and wipe over the sandals, then he said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do as you saw me do, I would have deemed the soles of the feet more deserving of wiping than their tops."
"1265","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There is no zakat on wealth until a year passes over it."
"1266","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: The Shiah claim that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, will return. He said: Those liars lie; had we known that, his wives would not have married nor would we have divided his inheritance."
"1267","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have exempted you from charity on horses and slaves, and there is no charity in them."
"1268","Abdullah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to me, Amr ibn Uthman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Hafs Abu Umar narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zadham, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever recites the Quran and memorizes it by heart, he will intercede for ten of his household for whom the Fire has become due."
"1269","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishkab narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have exempted horses and slaves from charity."
"1270","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Salm Khalil ibn Salm narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Amr ibn Khalid, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Jibril came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: We do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog, and the dog belonged to al-Hasan and was in the house."
"1271","Abdullah narrated to us, Ismail Abu Mamar narrated to me, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Ubad, he said: I said to Ali: Do you see this march of yours, is it a covenant the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to you, or an opinion you held? He said: What do you want with this? I said: Our religion, our religion. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not entrust to me anything concerning it, but it is an opinion I held."
"1272","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah had a spear, and when we went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a campaign, he would go out with it and plant it, and people would pass by it and carry it off. So I said: If I come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I will inform him. So he said: If you do, you will not restore a lost item."
"1273","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, performed ablution three times three times, then he drank the remainder of his ablution water, then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution."
"1274","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi Hafsah, he said: It reached me from Abdullah ibn Mulayl, so I went to him in the morning and found them at a funeral, so a man narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Mulayl, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Every prophet was given seven noble men, and your Prophet was given fourteen noble men, among them Abu Bakr and Umar and Abdullah ibn Masud and Ammar ibn Yasir."
"1275","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from Shurayh ibn al-Numan, and he was a truthful man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to examine the eye and the ear, and not to sacrifice a one-eyed animal, nor a muqabalah, nor a mudabarah, nor a sharqa, nor a kharqa. Zuhayr said: So I said to Abu Ishaq: Did he mention an adba? He said: No. I said: What is muqabalah? He said: It is that whose ear tip is cut. I said: Then what is mudabarah? He said: That whose back of the ear is cut. I said: What is sharqa? He said: That whose ear is split. I said: Then what is kharqa? He said: That whose ear the brand pierces."
"1276","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that you keep the meat of sacrifices beyond three days."
"1277","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani, he said: I asked Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about wiping over leather socks, so she said: Ask Ali, for he knows more about this than me; he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For the resident a day and a night, and for the traveler three days and their nights."
"1278","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, Hafs ibn Sulayman, meaning Abu Umar the reciter, narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zadham, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever learns the Quran and memorizes it by heart and preserves it, Allah will admit him to Paradise and grant him intercession for ten of his household, all of whom deserved the Fire."
"1279","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna, from al-Hakam, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to sacrifice two rams on his behalf, so I love to do it. And Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi said in his hadith: He sacrificed two rams on his behalf, one for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the other for himself. So it was said to him, so he said: He commanded me, so I will never abandon it."
"1280","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Awn ibn Abi Awn narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as a judge and said: When the two litigants come to you, do not judge against one of them until you hear from the other, for it will make the judgment clear to you."
"1281","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to me, and Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah al-Hadrami narrated to us, and Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen as a judge, so I said: You send me to a people while I am young in age and have no knowledge of judging, so he placed his hand upon my chest and said: May Allah make you firm and guide you. When the two litigants come to you, do not judge for the first until you hear from the other, for it is more likely to make the judgment clear to you. He said: So I have remained a judge ever since. And this is the wording of the hadith of Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi, and some of them are more complete in speech than others."
"1282","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as a judge to Yemen, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: Allah will make your heart firm and guide your conscience, then he mentioned the hadith."
"1283","Luwayn said: And Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with similar meaning."
"1284","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, al-Sakan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Ibn Ashwa, from Hanash al-Kinani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he sent his police officer and said to him: Do you know with what I send you? With what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me: That I carve away every image, meaning, and level every grave."
"1285","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: When two men bring their dispute to you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says, for you will see how to judge."
"1286","Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna, from al-Hakam, from Hanash, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sacrificing two rams, so I said to him: What is this? So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enjoined upon me to sacrifice on his behalf."
"1287","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to me, Amr ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Asbat ibn Nasr, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sent him with Baraah, he said: O Prophet of Allah, I am neither eloquent of tongue nor an orator. He said: It must be that I go with it or you go with it. He said: If it must be, then I will go. He said: Go, for Allah will make your tongue firm and guide your heart. He said: Then he placed his hand upon his mouth."
"1288","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, that Asim ibn Bahdalah said: I heard Zirr narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said on the day of Uhud: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their graves and their houses and their bellies with fire."
"1289","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of usury and its feeder and its two witnesses and its writer, and the tattooer and the one tattooed, and the muhill and the one for whom it is done, and the withholder of charity, and he forbade wailing."
"1290","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Nujayy narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I had an hour with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at night, through which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, nor a dog, nor one in major impurity. He said: So I looked, and there was a puppy of al-Hasan ibn Ali beneath the bed, so I removed it."
"1291","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard Abu Burdah narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me to place the ring on the middle finger."
"1292","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, delivering a sermon, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not lie upon me, for whoever lies upon me will enter the Fire."
"1293","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, that he heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb narrating that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the horn-broken and ear-broken sacrificial animal."
"1294","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Nahdi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sacrificing a horn-broken or ear-broken animal."
"1295","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amr al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I do not encompass praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"1296","Abdullah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali al-Azdi narrated to me, my father informed me, from Abu Sallam Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim ibn Sallam, from Imran ibn Zabyan, from Hukaym ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he intended a journey, said: O Allah, by You I attack and by You I move and by You I travel."
"1297","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When ten verses of Baraah were revealed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and sent him with them to recite them to the people of Makkah, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said to me: Catch up with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and wherever you meet him, take the document from him and go with it to the people of Makkah and recite it to them. So I met him at al-Juhfah and took the document from him, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, has anything been revealed concerning me? He said: No, but Jibril came to me and said: None shall convey on your behalf except you or a man of you."
"1298","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: It was said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Your Messenger used to single you out with something apart from the people generally. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not single us out with anything he did not single out the people with, except something in the sheath of this sword of mine. So he produced a sheet containing something about the teeth of camels, and therein: Madinah is sacred between Thawr and Air; whoever innovates therein an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; no obligatory nor voluntary deed will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection. And the protection of the Muslims is one, so whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; no obligatory nor voluntary deed will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever takes clients without permission of their masters, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; no obligatory nor voluntary deed will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1299","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said on the day of al-Ahzab: They detained us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer, until the sun set; may Allah fill their graves and their houses, or their graves and their bellies, with fire. Shubah said: May Allah fill their graves and their houses, or their graves and their bellies, with fire; I do not know whether it is in the hadith or not in the hadith; I doubt it."
"1300","Abdullah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mazin, that a man asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: O Commander of the Believers, describe to us the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; depict him for us. So he said: He was neither excessively tall nor short, above average; when he came with the people, he towered over them; white, intensely bright; large-headed; radiant, with a clear brow; long-lashed; thick-handed and thick-footed; when he walked, he lifted his feet as if descending a slope; as if sweat on his face were pearls; I never saw before him nor after him the like of him. May my father and mother be ransomed for him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1301","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mazin, from a man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that it was said to him: Describe the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for us, so he said: He was not excessively tall, then he mentioned the like of it exactly."
"1302","Abdullah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There were idols upon the Kabah, so I went to carry the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to them but I could not, so he carried me, and I began cutting them down, and if I had wished I would have reached the sky."
"1303","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythama narrated to me, Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim narrated to me, Abu Maryam narrated to me, Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A people will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game; they recite the Quran not passing their throats; blessed is he who kills them and whom they kill; their sign is a man with a defective arm."
"1304","Abdullah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, they said, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the wife of al-Walid ibn Uqba came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Walid beats her, and Nasr ibn Ali said in his hadith: complaining of him; he said: Say to him: He has granted me protection. Ali said: She stayed only a short while until she returned and said: He has only increased me in beating. So he took an edge of his garment and gave it to her and said: Say to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has granted me protection. She stayed only a short while until she returned and said: He has only increased me in beating. So he raised his hands and said: O Allah, deal with al-Walid; he has sinned against me twice. And this is the wording of the hadith of al-Qawariri, and their meaning is one."
"1305","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Abu Khaythama narrated to me, they said, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim informed us, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, that the wife of al-Walid ibn Uqba came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, complaining of al-Walid that he beats her, then he mentioned the hadith."
"1306","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that on the day of al-Ahzab he was at a pass of the trench passes, and he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their graves and their houses, or their bellies and their houses, with fire."
"1307","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said, I heard al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazza narrating from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, single you out with anything? So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not single us out with anything he did not include all the people in, except what was in the sheath of this sword of mine. He said: So he brought out a sheet in which was written: Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah; Allah has cursed whoever steals the landmarks of the earth; Allah has cursed whoever curses his father; and Allah has cursed whoever shelters an innovator."
"1308","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Hassan al-Araj, from Abida, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of al-Ahzab: O Allah, fill their houses and their graves with fire as they distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun returned."
"1309","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, he said, I heard Hujayya ibn Adi, he said, I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and a man asked him about the cow, so he said: For seven. And he asked him about the lame, so he said: When it reaches the rite. And he was asked about the horn, so he said: It does not harm it. And Ali said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear."
"1310","Bahz and Affan, the meaning, said, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Simak informed us, from Hanash ibn al-Mutamir, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was in Yemen, and they dug a pit for a lion, and a man came until he fell into it and clung to another, and the other clung to another, and the other clung to another, until they became four, and the lion wounded them in it; among them were those who died in it and among them were those who were taken out then died. He said: So they disputed about that until they took up arms. He said: So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came to them and said: Woe to you, will you kill two hundred people concerning four persons? Come, I will judge between you with a judgment; if you accept it, otherwise refer it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he judged for the first a quarter of blood-money, and for the second a third of blood-money, and for the third half of blood-money, and for the fourth the full blood-money. He said: So some of them accepted and some disliked it, and he placed the blood-money upon the tribes of those who crowded. He said: So they referred it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Bahz said, Hammad said, I think he said: He was reclining then sat up. He said: I will judge between you with a judgment. He said: So he was informed that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, had judged with such and such. He said: So he upheld his judgment. Affan said: I will judge between you."
"1311","Abdullah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Shair narrated to me, Shababa narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim narrated to me, Abu Maryam and a man from among the companions of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, from Ali, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. He said: So the people added after: Befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"1312","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Salama ibn Kuhayl informed us, from Hujayya ibn Adi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about the cow, so he said: For seven. And he was asked about the broken-horned, so he said: No harm. And he was asked about lameness, so he said: As long as it reaches the rite. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to inspect the two eyes and the two ears."
"1313","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ward, from Ibn Abud, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: O Ibn Abud, do you know what is the right of food? He said: I said: And what is its right, O Ibn Abi Talib? He said: You say: In the name of Allah, O Allah, bless for us in what You have provided us. He said: And do you know what is its thanks when you finish? He said: I said: And what is its thanks? He said: You say: Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink. Then he said: Shall I not inform you about me and about Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her? She was the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she was among the dearest of his family to him, and she was my wife. So she ground with the hand-mill until the mill left a mark on her hand, and she drew water with the waterskin until the waterskin left a mark on her neck, and she swept the house until her clothes became dusty, and she kindled fire under the pot until her clothes became soiled, and she suffered harm from that. So captives or servants were brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I said to her: Go to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him for a servant to protect you from the heat of what you are in. So she went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and found servants with him, but she returned and did not ask him. Then he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than a servant? When you go to your bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times and praise Allah thirty-three times and magnify Allah thirty-four times. He said: So she brought out her head and said: I am pleased with Allah and His Messenger, twice. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Ulayya from al-Jurayri or the like of it."
"1314","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Hassan, from Abida, he said: We used to think that the middle prayer was the dawn prayer. He said: So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us that on the day of al-Ahzab they fought and detained us from the afternoon prayer, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, fill their graves with fire, or fill their bellies with fire, as they detained us from the middle prayer. He said: So we knew on that day that the middle prayer is the afternoon prayer."
"1315","Bahz narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara informed me, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him a striped silk robe, so he wore it and went out to the people, and he recognized anger on his face, so he ordered him to divide it among his women."
"1316","Bahz narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, he said, I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, pray noon then sit for the needs of the people, and when afternoon came a vessel of water was brought, so he took a handful from it and wiped his face and his forearms and his head and his feet, then he took what remained and drank it standing, and said: People dislike this, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, doing it; and this is the ablution of one who has not broken it."
"1317","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from al-Shabi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Sharaha: Perhaps you were coerced; perhaps your husband came to you; perhaps you. She said: No. So when she gave birth he lashed her then stoned her. So it was said to him: Why did you lash her then stone her? He said: I lashed her by the Book of Allah and stoned her by the practice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1318","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Kamil Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, they said, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of you are those who learn the Quran and teach it."
"1319","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Wail, he said: A man came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am unable to pay my manumission contract, so help me. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not teach you words the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me? If there were upon you dinars like Mount Sir, Allah would pay it for you. I said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your unlawful and enrich me by Your bounty from all besides You."
"1320","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, they said, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"1321","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with Abu Musa, then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came to us and stood over Abu Musa and commanded him with a matter of the people's affairs. He said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Say: O Allah, guide me and set me straight, and recall by guidance Your guiding of the road, and recall by straightness the straightening of the arrow. And he forbade me to put my ring on this, and Abu Burda pointed to the forefinger or the middle; Asim said: I am the one who was confused as to which of them he meant. And he forbade me from the saddle-cloth and the Qassi garments. Abu Burda said: So I said to the Commander of the Faithful: What is the saddle-cloth and what is the Qassi? He said: As for the saddle-cloth, it is something women used to make for their husbands, placing it upon their saddles; and as for the Qassi, they are garments that used to come to us from Syria or Yemen, Asim doubted, in them is silk, in them are like citron patterns. Abu Burda said: So when I saw the Sabani I knew that it is it."
"1322","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, he said: A man said to Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, which month do you command me to fast after Ramadan? So he said: I have not heard anyone ask about this except after a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which month do you command me to fast after Ramadan? So he said: If you fast a month after Ramadan, then fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it is a day in which He forgave a people and will forgive in it other people."
"1323","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, and Amr al-Naqid narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"1324","Affan narrated to us, I think from Abu Awana, from Khalid ibn Alqama, from Abd Khayr, he said: I came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he had prayed, then he called for purification water, so we said: What will he do with purification water when he has prayed? He only intends to teach us. So a basin and a vessel were brought, so he raised the vessel and poured upon his hand and washed it three times, then he dipped his hand in the vessel and rinsed his mouth and nose three times, then he rinsed and blew from the palm he took from, then he washed his face three times and washed his right hand three times and his left hand three times, then he put his hand in the water and wiped his head once, then he washed his right foot three times and his left foot three times, then he said: Whoever is pleased to know the purification of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then it is this."
"1325","Muadh narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiya Abu Khaythama informed us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to stand over his sacrificial camels and to give in charity their meat and their skins and their coverings, and not to give the butcher from them. He said: We give him from ourselves."
"1326","Muadh narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me the like of this, except that he did not say: We give him from ourselves."
"1327","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada informed us, from Abu Hassan, from Abida al-Salmani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of al-Ahzab: May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire as they detained us from the middle prayer until the sun set, or he said: until the sun returned, one of the two phrases."
"1328","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Zabyan al-Janbi, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought a woman who had committed adultery, so he ordered her stoning, so they went with her to stone her, then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, met them and said: What is this? They said: She committed adultery, so Umar ordered her stoning. So Ali took her from their hands and turned them back, so they returned to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: What turned you back? They said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, turned us back. He said: Ali did not do this except for something he knew. So he sent to Ali, and he came while almost angry, and said: Why did you turn these back? He said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he grows, and from the afflicted until he recovers his mind? He said: Yes. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Then this is the afflicted woman of the sons of so-and-so; perhaps he came to her while with her. So Umar said: I do not know. He said: And I do not know. So he did not stone her."
"1329","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, and Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin narrated to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"1330","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, as raised: That he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade reciting the Quran while bowing, and said: When you bow, magnify Allah, and when you prostrate, supplicate, for it is likely to be answered for you."
"1331","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Mamar narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir and Abu Muawiya narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"1332","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, he said: Abida said: I will not narrate to you except what I heard from him. Muhammad said: So Abida swore to us three times, and Ali swore to him: Were it not that you would exult, I would inform you of what Allah has promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. Among them is a man with a defective arm, or small-handed, I think he said, or with a malformed arm."
"1333","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, al-Numan ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he recited this verse: On the day We gather the God-fearing to the Merciful as a delegation. He said: No, by Allah, they will not be gathered upon their feet, nor is a delegation gathered upon their feet, but upon she-camels the creatures have never seen the like of, upon them saddles of gold, so they will ride upon them until they knock at the gates of Paradise."
"1334","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ikrima, he said: I stood with al-Husayn, and I kept hearing him say: Here I am, until he stoned the jamra. So I said: O Abu Abd Allah, what is this calling? He said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, calling until he reached the jamra, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called until he reached it."
"1335","Abdullah narrated to us, Zuhayr Abu Khaythama narrated to me, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a month I fast after Ramadan. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you fast a month after Ramadan, then fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it is a day in which He forgave a people and will be forgiven in it for others."
"1336","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: People of Quraysh came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Muhammad, we are your neighbors and allies, and people of our slaves have come to you, having no desire for religion nor desire for understanding; they only fled from our estates and our wealth, so return them to us. So he said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: What do you say? He said: They spoke truthfully; they are your neighbors. He said: So the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed. Then he said to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: What do you say? He said: They spoke truthfully; they are your neighbors and allies. So the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed."
"1337","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me in the year two hundred twenty-six, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man asked him: Shall I recite in bowing and prostration? So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been forbidden to recite in bowing and prostration; so when you bow, magnify Allah, and when you prostrate, strive in asking, for it is likely to be answered for you."
"1338","Abdullah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi Abu Muhammad narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In Paradise there are chambers whose insides are seen from their outsides and whose outsides are seen from their insides. So a Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, for whom are they? He said: For whoever makes speech good and feeds food and prays to Allah at night while people sleep."
"1339","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, and Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to me, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, all from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"1340","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abdullah ibn Sabu, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: By Him who split the seed and created the soul, this will surely be dyed from this. He said: The people said: So inform us who he is; by Allah we will surely destroy his kin. He said: I adjure you by Allah that none be killed but my killer. They said: If you know that, then appoint a successor. He said: No, but I leave you to what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left you to."
"1341","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zaida informed us, from al-Suddi, from Sad ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us, he said: O people, carry out the prescribed penalties upon your slaves, those of them who were married and those who were not, for a slave-girl of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, committed adultery, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to carry out the penalty upon her. So I came to her and she was newly delivered of childbirth, so I feared if I lashed her she would die. So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so he said: You did well."
"1342","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, so I said: You send me to a people while they are older than I to judge between them. So he said: Go, for Allah will guide your heart and steady your tongue."
"1343","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In Paradise there is a market with no buying nor selling in it except images of women and men; so when a man desires an image he enters into it. And in it is a gathering for the wide-eyed maidens raising voices the creatures have never seen the like of, saying: We are the eternal, so we do not perish; and we are the pleased, so we do not anger; and we are the blissful, so we do not suffer. So blessed is he who was for us and we were for him."
"1344","Abdullah narrated to us, Zuhayr Abu Khaythama narrated to me, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In Paradise there is a market, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: When a man desires an image he enters it. He said: And in it is a gathering of the wide-eyed maidens raising voices, then he mentioned the like of it."
"1345","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya ibn Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he performed ablution three times three times, then wiped his head, then drank the remainder of his ablution, then said: Whoever is pleased to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then let him look at this."
"1346","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Suwayd ibn Ghafala, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be at the end of time a people reciting the Quran not passing their throats; they pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game; fighting them is a duty upon every Muslim."
"1347","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Haritha ibn al-Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the fighting grew fierce and the people met the people, we sought protection with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and none of us was closer to the enemy than he."
"1348","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at Arafat and said: This is the stopping place, and all of Arafat is a stopping place. Then he took Usama behind him and made his camel trot, and the people were beating camels right and left, not turning to them, saying: Calmness, O people. And he moved when the sun set, then came to Jam, and prayed in it the two prayers, meaning sunset and nightfall, then spent the night in it. When morning came he stopped at Quzah and said: This is Quzah, and it is the stopping place, and all of Jam is a stopping place. He said: Then he went, and when he came to Muhassir he spurred her and she trotted until she crossed the valley, then he restrained her and took al-Fadl behind him, then went until he came to the jamra and stoned it, then came to the slaughter place and said: This is the slaughter place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place. Then a young woman of Khatham came to him and said: My father is an old man who has become senile, and the obligation of Allah in pilgrimage has reached him; will it suffice to perform pilgrimage for him? He said: Yes, so perform for your father. He said: And he twisted the neck of al-Fadl, so al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you twist the neck of your cousin? He said: I saw a young man and a young woman, so I feared Satan for them. He said: And a man came to him and said: I hastened before shaving. He said: So shave or shorten, and no harm. He said: And he came to Zamzam and said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, your watering; were it not that people would overpower you over it, I would have drawn."
"1349","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Barid, narrated to us, from Ismail al-Hanafi, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, took my hand, and we went walking until we sat upon the bank of the Euphrates. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no breathed soul but Allah has already decreed for it misery or happiness. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, for what then do we act? He said: Act, for each is facilitated to what he was created for. Then he recited this verse: As for he who gives and fears and believes in the best, to His saying: So We will facilitate him to hardship."
"1350","Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya al-Wadii, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, urinate in the open ground, then call for water and perform ablution; so he washed his palms three times and rinsed his mouth and nose three times and washed his face three times and washed his forearms three times three times and wiped his head and washed his feet three times three times, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do as you saw me do."
"1351","Abdullah narrated to us, Zuhayr Abu Khaythama narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution three times three times."
"1352","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution; so he cleaned his palms, then washed his face three times and his forearms three times and wiped his head, then washed his feet to the ankles, then stood and drank the remainder of his ablution, then said: I only intended to show you the purification of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1353","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi, Abu Matar al-Basri narrated to me, and he had met Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that Ali bought a garment for three dirhams, and when he wore it he said: Praise be to Allah who provided me of adornment what I beautify myself with among people and cover my nakedness with, then he said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say."
"1354","Abdullah narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya al-Hamdani, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Whoever is pleased to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then let him look at me. He said: So he performed ablution three times three times, then wiped his head, then drank the remainder of his ablution."
"1355","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Nafi al-Tammar narrated to us, from Abu Matar, that he saw Ali come to a young servant and buy from him a shirt for three dirhams, and wear it to between the wrists to the ankles, saying, and he wore it: Praise be to Allah who provided me of adornment what I beautify myself with among people and cover my nakedness with. So it was said: Is this something you narrate from yourself or from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: This is something I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say at clothing: Praise be to Allah who provided me of adornment what I beautify myself with among people and cover my nakedness with."
"1356","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Mukhtar, from Abu Matar, he said: While we were sitting with the Commander of the Faithful, Ali, in the mosque at the door of al-Rahba, a man came and said: Show me the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was at midday. So he called Qanbar and said: Bring me a jug of water. So he washed his palms and his face three times and rinsed three times, putting some of his fingers in his mouth, and sniffed three times, and washed his forearms three times, and wiped his head once. So he said: Their insides from the face and their outsides from the head, and his feet to the ankles three times, and his beard dripping upon his chest. Then he sipped a sip after ablution, then said: Where is the questioner about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Such was the ablution of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1357","Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said, Misar narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I did not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combine his father and his mother for anyone except for Sad. Abu Nuaym said: His two parents, for anyone."
"1358","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you select among Quraysh and not marry to us? He said: And do you have anything? He said: I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamza. He said: That is the daughter of my brother by nursing."
"1359","Abu Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A mule was gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he rode it. So some of his companions said: If we took the like of this. He said: Do you want to breed donkeys upon horses? Only those who do not know do that."
"1360","Abdullah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid narrated to me, al-Ala ibn Hilal al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not show you how the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution? We said: Yes. He said: So bring me a basin and a vessel of water. So he washed his hands three times and sniffed three times and blew three times and washed his face three times and washed his hands to the elbows three times and wiped his head three times and washed his feet three times."
"1361","Abu Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Zabyan, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Umar: O Commander of the Faithful, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he grows, and from the afflicted until he recovers his mind?"
"1362","Abu Said narrated to us, Said ibn Salama ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Akbar, that he heard his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been given four none of the prophets of Allah were given: I have been given the keys of the earth, and I was named Ahmad, and dust was made for me a purification, and my nation was made the best of nations."
"1363","Abu Said narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not teach you words, when you say them you will be forgiven, though you are forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the High, the Mighty; there is no god but He, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1364","Abu Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of usury and its giver and its two witnesses and its writer, and the legalizer and the one for whom it is legalized, and the tattooer and the tattooed, and the withholder of charity, and forbade wailing."
"1365","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sins a sin in this world and is punished for it, then Allah is more just than to repeat His punishment upon His servant; and whoever sins a sin in this world and Allah covers him and pardons him, then Allah is more generous than to return to something He has pardoned."
"1366","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythama narrated to me, and Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, they said, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, he said: We prayed with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, noon, then he went to a sitting place of his where he sits in al-Rahba, so he sat and we sat around him, then afternoon came, so a vessel was brought, so he took a handful from it and rinsed his mouth and sniffed and wiped his face and his forearms and wiped his head and wiped his feet, then stood and drank the remainder of his vessel, then said: I was told that men dislike that one of them drink while standing; I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do as I did."
"1367","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while I tie a stone upon my belly from hunger, and my charity today is forty thousand."
"1368","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, then he mentioned the hadith, and he said in it: And the charity of my wealth reaches forty thousand dinars."
"1369","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Salama ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do not follow a glance with a glance, for the first is for you and the last is not for you."
"1370","Zakariya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When al-Hasan was born he named him Hamza, and when al-Husayn was born he named him by his uncle Jafar. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said: I have been commanded to change the names of these two. So I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So he named them Hasan and Husayn."
"1371","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabia ibn Najidh, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gathered, or called, the sons of Abd al-Muttalib, among them a group each of whom eats the young camel and drinks the faraq. He said: So he made for them a mudd of food, so they ate until they were full. He said: And the food remained as it was as if untouched. Then he called for a cup and they drank until satisfied, and the drink remained as if untouched or undrunk. So he said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, I have been sent to you specially and to people generally, and you have seen of this sign what you have seen, so which of you will pledge me to be my brother and companion? He said: So none stood to him. He said: So I stood to him, and I was the youngest of the people. He said: So he said: Sit. He said: Three times, each time I stand to him and he says to me: Sit, until at the third he struck his hand upon my hand."
"1372","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he drank while standing, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1373","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Salama ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Ali, you have a treasure from Paradise, and you are its possessor; so do not follow a glance with a glance, for the first is for you and the last is not for you."
"1374","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtered his sacrificial camels, he slaughtered thirty by his hand and ordered me so I slaughtered the rest, and said: Divide their meat among people, and their skins and their coverings, and do not give a butcher anything from them."
"1375","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said, I heard Asim ibn Damra say: We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in daytime, so he said: You cannot bear that. We said: Whoever of us can bear that. He said: When the sun is from here like it is from here at afternoon, he prayed two units, and when the sun is from here like it is from here at noon, he prayed four, and he prays before noon four and after it two, and before afternoon four, and separates between every two units by greeting upon the near angels and the prophets and those who follow them of the believers and the Muslims."
"1376","Abu Abd al-Rahman said, Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to me, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Harith ibn Hasira, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabia ibn Najidh, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: In you is a likeness of Jesus: the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him at a rank he does not have. Then he said: Two men perish concerning me: an excessive lover praising me with what is not in me, and a hater whose hatred of me carries him to slander me."
"1377","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Muhammad Sufyan ibn Waki ibn al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to me, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abu Ghaylan al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Harith ibn Hasira, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabia ibn Najid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said: In you is a likeness of Jesus: the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him at a rank he does not have. Verily two perish concerning me: a lover praising me with what is not in me, and a hater whose hatred of me carries him to slander me. Verily I am not a prophet nor is revelation given to me, but I act by the Book of Allah and the practice of His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as much as I can; so whatever I command you of obedience to Allah, obedience to me is due upon you in what you love and hate."
"1378","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to me, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, he said: I was sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was none with him except Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, so he said: O Ibn Abi Talib, how are you with people of such and such? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A people coming out from the east reciting the Quran not passing their throats, passing out of religion as the arrow passes out of the game; among them is a man with a defective arm as if his hands are an Abyssinian breast."
"1379","Abdullah narrated to us, Ismail Abu Mamar narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, he said: I was sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when a man in travel clothes entered upon him and sought permission from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was speaking to people, so he was distracted from him. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with him was Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, so he said to me: How are you with people of such and such? So I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then he repeated, so I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: So he said: A people coming out from the east reciting the Quran not passing their throats, passing out of religion as the arrow passes out of the game; among them is a man with a defective arm as if his hand is an Abyssinian breast. I adjure you by Allah, did I not inform you that among them, then he mentioned the hadith in full."
"1380","Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya al-Wadii, from Amr Dhu Murr, he said: We saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution; so he washed his hands and rinsed his mouth and sniffed, he said, and I doubt about rinsing and sniffing three times, whether he mentioned it or not, and washed his face three times and his hands three times, each of them three times, and wiped his head and his ears, he said, one of them, then took a handful and wiped his head with it, then stood and drank the remainder of his ablution, then said: Thus the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution. End of the musnad of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
